{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_16","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"cat /Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/collab/dao-stream/1794147282000-engineer-step1-invariant-pins.muse-wonder-1.0.stdout.log; cat /Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/collab/dao-stream/1794147282000-engineer-step1-invariant-pins.prompt.md; rg --files --hidden --no-ignore target | rg '(log\"'$|step|result|summary)'\"' | head -60\"","aggregated_output":"muse: workspace root: /Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-yin-repl-dht (cwd default)\nmuse: workspace trust: trusted source=run-flag\nmuse: warning: rules file at /Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-yin-repl-dht/CLAUDE.md is ignored this session because AGENTS.md takes precedence in that directory; merge still-applicable guidance into AGENTS.md or remove one of the two files\nmuse: Skills: 38 loaded · 1 warning\nmuse:   `skills_catalog` was trimmed to fit its size limit (32 KB): 1 descriptions compacted, 0 skill ids omitted\nmuse:   Run `muse skills list --source all` for full diagnostics.\nCompleted-GMT: 2026-11-08 14:37:44 GMT\nCompleted-Local: 2026-11-08 21:37:44 +07\n\nStep 1 is complete. Existing invariants are green and the publication-result expectations are now explicit, with all changes contained in `test/yin/repl/` and no `src/` edits (uncommitted, for review).\n\n**Modified files**\n\n- [fixture.cljc](/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-yin-repl-dht/test/yin/repl/fixture.cljc) (new) — Gate B's common test constructor: explicitly injected non-DHT backends (`:memory` via `dao.jing.mem/create-content-mem`, `:file` via `dao.space.store/open`), the composition-side publication interpreter (`observed-backend`/`failable-backend` wrapping `:head-fn`), and `frontier` extraction (manifest identity, count, count-cap, cursor). It requires no DHT namespace and constructs no node, socket, follower, or scheduler.\n- [index_test.cljc](/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-yin-repl-dht/test/yin/repl/index_test.cljc) — decisive publication/frontier/recovery tests (§8; spec lines 146, 269, 316, 344, 362, 385, 421, 470, 501, 522, 576) parameterized over both backends, plus six new pins: frontier-gate agreement after every round, correlated settle-once publication requests, failed-HEAD never advancing the frontier, count-cap mismatch forcing full reconstruction, exact suffix length, and no double settlement.\n- [require_test.cljc](/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-yin-repl-dht/test/yin/repl/require_test.cljc) — `shell`/`require-and-apply` now take the injected backend; prompt-path and rollback tests run on both backends; remaining causality/policy tests use explicit memory injection via `prompt-state`; the DHT composition test (was line 805) is isolated as composition-side for its Step 2 move, still green.\n- [query_test.cljc](/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-yin-repl-dht/test/yin/repl/query_test.cljc) — all shells built through the fixture; settlement tests (283, slow 314, 663) and the basic answer test run on every VM × backend.\n- [store_test.cljc](/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-yin-repl-dht/test/yin/repl/store_test.cljc) — new cross-backend proof: same programs publish agreeing frontiers and identical history (modulo session token) on either backend, with `(:dht state)` and `(:index-store-spec state)` both nil.\n\n**Diff summary:** 4 files changed, 1022 insertions, 505 deletions, plus the new fixture (212 lines). `git status` shows only these test files; no commits made.\n\n**Focused test outcomes** (JVM, run individually, `-e :slow` except the one slow var)\n\n| Suite | Baseline | Final |\n|---|---|---|\n| `yin.repl.index-test` | 21 tests, 242 assertions | 27 tests, 569 assertions, 0 failures |\n| `yin.repl.require-test` | 20 tests, 172 assertions | 20 tests, 209 assertions, 0 failures |\n| `yin.repl.query-test` | 18 tests, 246 assertions | 18 tests, 279 assertions, 0 failures |\n| `yin.repl.store-test` | 27 tests, 132 assertions | 28 tests, 145 assertions, 0 failures |\n\nThe slow query settlement var also passes on both backends (16 assertions). Node/Dart lanes were not run (focused JVM runs only, per instructions); the fixture is reader-conditional portable, but that remains unverified. Generated ANTLR parser classes were seeded into the gitignored `build/` cache so the JVM lane could run at all; the working tree carries no build changes.\n\n**Finding for Step 2 (not pinned, not fixed — `src/` is out of Step 1 scope):** continuing the shell past a refused publication throws inside `yin.repl.index/notice`, which renders `(name stage)` of the cleared failure and rolls the round back. I verified this on unmodified engine code with a debug script; the failed-HEAD pin therefore proves the retry at the indexer level and documents the defect at the shell level.\nCreated-GMT: 2026-11-08 14:14:42 GMT\nCreated-Local: 2026-11-08 21:14:42 +07\nCoding-Agent: muse\nSession-ID: e8c6e6a5-b58b-45ac-914b-a696f4512f9e\n\n# Task: Pin baseline contracts and parameterize non-DHT fixtures (Step 1)\n\nRole: DaoSpace and DaoJing Storage Engineer\n\nImplementers:\n- Model: muse-wonder-1.0 | Assigned: 2026-11-08 21:14:42 +07 | Status: active | Rationale: Step 1 of spec §9 commit sequence; dedicated scratch worktree datomworld-yin-repl-dht\n\n## Governing Specification & Instructions\nRead first:\n- `docs/design/yin.repl.dht-composition.md` (specifically §8 Invariants to pin before relocation, and §9 Commit sequence Step 1).\n- Existing fixtures referenced in spec §8:\n  - `test/yin/repl/index_test.cljc` (specifically lines around 385, 421, 470, 501, 553, 734)\n  - `test/yin/repl/require_test.cljc` (specifically lines around 244–766)\n  - `test/yin/repl/query_test.cljc` (specifically lines around 283, 314, 663)\n  - `test/yin/repl/store_test.cljc` (specifically lines around 833–1425)\n\n## Scope & Acceptance Criteria (Step 1 Exit Condition)\nExit condition: Existing invariants green; new publication-result expectations explicit.\n\n1. **Parameterize non-DHT fixtures:**\n   - For index, require, query, and store test fixtures that test engine behavior, ensure they can run against non-DHT storage handles (e.g. in-memory or generic file-backed `dao.jing` store) without requiring `dao.jing.dht`.\n2. **Make publication-result expectations explicit:**\n   - Establish explicit assertions for local publication request and correlated publication result records per spec §3 and §8 (Frontier gate: manifest identity, published transaction count, count-cap compatibility, cursor ownership, and expected suffix length; failed HEAD persistence must not advance the frontier).\n3. **Verify invariant baseline:**\n   - Keep changes strictly contained to `test/yin/repl/` (and any minimal non-DHT fixture helpers if required under `test/yin/`). Do NOT refactor the engine implementation in `src/` yet (that belongs to Step 2).\n   - Ensure existing tests pass or are cleanly parameterized.\n\n## Execution Rules\n- Work in `/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-yin-repl-dht` on branch `yin-repl-dht-composition`.\n- Do NOT commit your changes; leave them in the working tree for verification and review.\n- Run focused tests individually (e.g. `clojure -M:test -v ...`). Do not run full test suites locally.\n- Begin the final response exactly with:\nCompleted-GMT: <YYYY-MM-DD HH:MM:SS GMT>\nCompleted-Local: <YYYY-MM-DD HH:MM:SS local-timezone-name>\n- Report modified files, diff summary, and focused test outcomes.\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
