cell)\\\\nsrc/cljc/yin/vm/docs/yin.repl.md:454:A require whose closure the node does not hold prints the\\\\nsrc/cljc/yin/vm/docs/yin.repl.md:456:closure from the peers, the parked require is re-checked when the load\\\\nsrc/cljc/yin/vm/docs/yin.repl.md:505:and the closure walk re-checks the manifest, every tree row, every\\\\nsrc/cljc/yin/vm/docs/yin.repl.md:529:`yin.vm.linker.dht/load-module` for a module's closure, and\\\\ntest/yang/python/antlr/e2e_c1_test.clj:254:            closures over the loop variable share its one cell\\\\\\\"\\\\nsrc/cljc/yin/vm/ledger.cljc:162:      `validate-rows`, every row is the reachable closure — and the\\\\ntest/yang/python/antlr/import_test.cljc:112:      (is (= '#{yang.call py} (required-modules program))))\\\\ntest/yang/python/antlr/import_test.cljc:142:      (is (= '#{yang.call py} (required-modules program)))\\\\ntest/yang/python/antlr/import_test.cljc:188:      (is (= '[yang.call py] (requires-of program)))\\\\ntest/yang/python/antlr/import_test.cljc:290:      (is (= '[yang.call py]\\\\ntest/yang/python/antlr/import_test.cljc:317:      (is (= '[yang.call py] (requires-of program))))\\\\ntest/yang/python/antlr/import_test.cljc:362:      (is (= '[yang.call py] (requires-of program)))\\\\ntest/yang/python/antlr/import_test.cljc:421:      (is (= '#{yang.call py} (required-modules program))))))\\\\ntest/yang/python/antlr/import_test.cljc:1328:    (is (= '[yang.call py] (requires-of ast)))\\\\ntest/yang/python/antlr/linked_prelude_test.cljc:142:    (is (= {'yang.call :test/call-address} (:requires spec)))\\\\ntest/yang/python/antlr/linked_prelude_test.cljc:538:        (is (= 'yang.call (:name refusal)))\\\\nsrc/cljc/yin/vm/docs/summary.md:11:- ✅ Lambda expressions (closures)\\\\nsrc/cljc/yin/vm/docs/summary.md:66:Step  2: ctrl=nil          cont=:eval-operator  val=<closure>\\\\nsrc/cljc/yin/vm/docs/summary.md:115:Values (literals, variables, closures) always return with `control` set to `nil`. The main eval loop then checks for pending continuations and applies them. This keeps the code clean and makes stepping explicit.\\\\nsrc/cljc/yin/vm/docs/summary.md:168:2. **Working lambda calculus** with closures and higher-order functions\\\\ntest/yang/python/antlr/dht_import_fixture.cljc:9:   their closures but `py`'s, which each reader has installed, and each\\\\ntest/yang/python/antlr/dht_import_fixture.cljc:37:    [yin.vm.linker.closure :as closure]\\\\ntest/yang/python/antlr/dht_import_fixture.cljc:62:(defn closure-addresses\\\\ntest/yang/python/antlr/dht_import_fixture.cljc:63:  \\\\\\\"Every blob address of the closure of `manifest` in `store`: the reads\\\\ntest/yang/python/antlr/dht_import_fixture.cljc:64:   one closure walk makes.\\\\\\\"\\\\ntest/yang/python/antlr/dht_import_fixture.cljc:73:    (closure/walk recording manifest)\\\\ntest/yang/python/antlr/dht_import_fixture.cljc:78:  \\\\\\\"`py`'s closure as this host published it, `{address bytes}`: the\\\\ntest/yang/python/antlr/dht_import_fixture.cljc:85:    (select-keys ((:entries-fn store)) (closure-addresses store address))))\\\\ntest/yang/python/antlr/dht_import_fixture.cljc:89:  \\\\\\\"`pysp`'s closure as this host published it, `{address bytes}`: the hook\\\\ntest/yang/python/antlr/dht_import_fixture.cljc:91:   (the closure includes `py`'s).\\\\\\\"\\\\ntest/yang/python/antlr/dht_import_fixture.cljc:95:        addresses (closure-addresses store pysp)]\\\\nsrc/cljc/yin/vm/docs/assignments.md:398:4. **Flexible** - Can handle loops, closures, etc.\\\\ntest/yang/python/antlr/dht_import_test.cljc:149:  \\\\\\\"Every node's inbound bound: py's closure is replicated whole.\\\\\\\"\\\\ntest/yang/python/antlr/lower_portable_test.cljc:146:    (testing \\\\\\\"require yang.call and py, allocate task state, run the body\\\\\\\"\\\\ntest/yang/python/antlr/lower_portable_test.cljc:148:               (u/seq-nodes [(u/app (u/v 'require) (u/lit 'yang.call))\\\\ntest/yang/python/antlr/int_heap_test.cljc:112:  (testing \\\\\\\"a closure whose environment holds every boundary integer: the\\\\ntest/yang/python/antlr/int_heap_test.cljc:114:            closure lowered into another task returns them unchanged, on\\\\ntest/yang/python/antlr/int_heap_test.cljc:125:          (is (values/closure? f) (str k))\\\\nsrc/cljc/yin/vm/docs/ast.md:168:  - Even functions (though typically functions are closures)\\\\nsrc/cljc/yin/vm/docs/ast.md:276:Lambdas are the primary mechanism for defining functions. When evaluated, a lambda node produces a **closure**—a value that combines the function's code with the environment in which it was created.\\\\nsrc/cljc/yin/vm/docs/ast.md:301:> an already-expanded ordinary closure whose source happened to be a macro\\\\nsrc/cljc/yin/vm/docs/ast.md:324:When the Yin VM encounters a lambda node, it doesn't execute the body. Instead, it creates a **closure**:\\\\nsrc/cljc/yin/vm/docs/ast.md:328:3. **Create Closure Value** - It mints a closure over the params, body, and the captured environment.\\\\nsrc/cljc/yin/vm/docs/ast.md:338:            (closure-of (:owner state) node params body env)))\\\\nsrc/cljc/yin/vm/docs/ast.md:343:A closure is a host type, `yin.vm.values/Closure` (D7), minted only by a kernel. It wraps the kernel's payload map and the owner tag of the task that minted it:\\\\nsrc/cljc/yin/vm/docs/ast.md:345:(values/closure owner\\\\nsrc/cljc/yin/vm/docs/ast.md:346:                {:type :closure\\\\nsrc/cljc/yin/vm/docs/ast.md:352:- **Unforgeable.** `values/closure?` is a type test. A guest map carrying `:type :closure` is data: applying it refuses `:not-applicable`, and the lift encoder wraps it as a literal.\\\\nsrc/cljc/yin/vm/docs/ast.md:354:- **Owned.** The owner tag is derived once per task from its capability secret (`values/owner-tag`, held in VM state as `:owner`; nil for a task without a secret). Application refuses a closure another task minted with `:foreign-value`. Lift is the only crossing: the encoder refuses a foreign closure as `:yin.k/non-portable` of kind `:foreign-value`, and `lower-closure` mints with the receiver's owner. A lower takes its binders from the attached lambda, never the wire: a marker whose `:yin.k/params` (named kernels) or `:yin.k/arity` (positional kernels) is not the attached lambda's refuses `:marker-mismatch`, and a non-symbol binder refuses `:non-symbol-parameter` first.\\\\nsrc/cljc/yin/vm/docs/ast.md:355:- **Equal by structure.** `=` compares kind, owner and payload, and `hash` agrees, so two runs of one program give equal VM states and a closure can be a set member. A closure never equals its payload map.\\\\nsrc/cljc/yin/vm/docs/ast.md:356:- **Opaque in print.** Every host rendering (`str`, `pr-str`, guest `print`/`println`/`prn`, the REPL display, nested inside a collection) is the kind marker `{:type :closure}` or `{:type :continuation}`, shaped like the `{:type :host-fn}` marker: never the payload, a captured value, or the owner tag.\\\\nsrc/cljc/yin/vm/docs/ast.md:364:- 🏗️ **Deferred Execution** - The body is only evaluated when the closure is applied (see Part 4).\\\\nsrc/cljc/yin/vm/docs/ast.md:389:- `:operator` - An AST node that, when evaluated, must yield a function (primitive or closure).\\\\nsrc/cljc/yin/vm/docs/ast.md:420:   - **If Closure**: The VM extends the closure's captured environment by binding `:params` to the argument values, then evaluates the closure's `:body` in this new environment.\\\\nsrc/cljc/yin/vm/docs/ast.md:443:    :closure (let [{:keys [params body], closure-env :env}\\\\nsrc/cljc/yin/vm/docs/ast.md:445:                   extended-env (merge closure-env\\\\nsrc/cljc/yin/vm/docs/ast.md:464:| `:not-applicable` | The operator is neither a host function, a closure nor a continuation. Carries a coarse `:kind` (`:number`, `:map`, ...), never the value. |\\\\nsrc/cljc/yin/vm/docs/ast.md:465:| `:foreign-value` | A closure or continuation another task minted. Carries `:kind :closure` or `:continuation`. |\\\\nsrc/cljc/yin/vm/docs/ast.md:683:- **Tracing, in two modes:** a cell ref marks its cell and traces its content. In a *kernel* position (a continuation register, an engine table entry, a closure or continuation payload, or a kernel child of one) a value of the kernel's own shape contributes what the kernel's `gc-children` answers, split into further kernel positions and values (a walker frame's `:evaluated` and `:fn`, never its operand subtrees). In a *value* position (an environment value, an operand, a value register, the store, a cell's content) every map is walked whole, so a guest map shaped like a frame never hides a cell ref; only a closure or continuation, which no guest can forge, re-enters kernel mode through its payload.\\\\nsrc/cljc/yin/vm/docs/ast.md:705:**Evaluation:** Returns a continuation value carrying the current continuation and lexical environment: a `yin.vm.values/Continuation` host type, minted only by a kernel and owned by the capturing task, over the `:reified-continuation` payload map. Like a closure (Part 3) it is unforgeable, opaque to guest `get`, equal by structure, and refused with `:foreign-value` in another task. A continuation never crosses a lift (`:non-canonicalizable`). A `:parked-continuation` stays plain data: resume goes by id through the engine's `:parked` table.\\\\nsrc/cljc/yin/vm/linker/requirements.cljc:2:  \\\\\\\"Derived module-level requirements, shared by publication and closure\\\\ntest/yang/python/antlr/siteset_test.cljc:353:    (testing \\\\\\\"a complete closure is written, the parent reading its child\\\\\\\"\\\\ntest/yang/core/call_test.cljc:65:                        '(yang.call/valid-invocation?\\\\ntest/yang/core/call_test.cljc:66:                           {:yang.call/callee :f\\\\ntest/yang/core/call_test.cljc:67:                            :yang.call/positional []\\\\ntest/yang/core/call_test.cljc:68:                            :yang.call/named [[\\\\\\\"x\\\\\\\" 1] [\\\\\\\"x\\\\\\\" 2]]\\\\ntest/yang/core/call_test.cljc:69:                            :yang.call/raise