   366\\\\\\\\tshards come from `bb test:sub:list <subsystem>` for the 13 subsystems that hold JVM\\\\\\\\n   367\\\\\\\\ttests, so each subsystem is one JVM; the script also checks that the shards cover every\\\\\\\\n   368\\\\\\\\tJVM test namespace under `test/`:\\\\\\\\n   369\\\\\\\\t\\\\\\\\n   370\\\\\\\\t```sh\\\\\\\\n   371\\\\\\\\t#!/usr/bin/env bash\\\\\\\\n   372\\\\\\\\t# Usage: shard-jvm.sh <clone> [parallel]  -- JVM lane sharded by subsystem (fast tests, -e :slow)\\\\\\\\n   373\\\\\\\\tset -u\\\\\\\\n   374\\\\\\\\texport PATH=\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"$HOME/.local/bin:/snap/bin:$PATH\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\\n   375\\\\\\\\tcd \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"$1\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\" || exit 2\\\\\\\\n   376\\\\\\\\tPAR=\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"${2:-8}\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\\n   377\\\\\\\\tmise trust >/dev/null 2>&1\\\\\\\\n   378\\\\\\\\teval \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"$(mise env -s bash)\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\\n   379\\\\\\\\tOUT=\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"$1/target-ci/shards\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"; rm -rf \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"$OUT\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"; mkdir -p \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"$OUT\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\\n   380\\\\\\\\tts() { date +%H:%M:%S; }\\\\\\\\n   381\\\\\\\\techo \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"start $(ts) $(git rev-parse --short HEAD) par=$PAR\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\" | tee \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"$OUT/summary.txt\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\\n   382\\\\\\\\tnpm ci --silent >\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"$OUT/npm.log\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\" 2>&1                   && echo \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"npm ok $(ts)\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\" | tee -a \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"$OUT/summary.txt\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\\n   383\\\\\\\\tbb build:yin-repl-node >\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"$OUT/build-node.log\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\" 2>&1     && echo \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"node repl built $(ts)\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\" | tee -a \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"$OUT/summary.txt\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\\n   384\\\\\\\\tbb gen:antlr >\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"$OUT/antlr.log\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\" 2>&1             && echo \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"antlr ok $(ts)\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\" | tee -a \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"$OUT/summary.txt\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\\n   385\\\\\\\\tSUBS=\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"yang.python yin.repl yin.vm yin.vm.ucf dao.stream dao.jing dao.gui dao.space demo dao.data dao.postgraphics yang.base dao.base\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\\n   386\\\\\\\\t: > \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"$OUT/covered.txt\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\\n   387\\\\\\\\tfor s in $SUBS; do\\\\\\\\n   388\\\\\\\\t  bb test:sub:list \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"$s\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\" 2>/dev/null | awk \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"/^clj:/{f=1;next} /^[A-Za-z]/{f=0} f{gsub(/ /,\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\");print}\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\" > \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"$OUT/ns-$s.txt\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\\n   389\\\\\\\\t  cat \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"$OUT/ns-$s.txt\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\" >> \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"$OUT/covered.txt\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\\n   390\\\\\\\\t  echo \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"$s $(wc -l < \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"$OUT/ns-$s.txt\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\")\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\" >> \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"$OUT/plan.txt\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\\n   391\\\\\\\\tdone\\\\\\\\n   392\\\\\\\\t# coverage: every JVM test namespace under test/ vs the union of the shards\\\\\\\\n   393\\\\\\\\tfind test -type f \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\( -name \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"*_test.clj\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\" -o -name \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"*_test.cljc\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\" \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\) | sed -e \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"s#^test/##\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\" -e \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"s#\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\.cljc\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\?\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\$##\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\" -e \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"s#/#.#g\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\" -e \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"s#_#-#g\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\" | sort -u > \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"$OUT/all.txt\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\\n   394\\\\\\\\tsort -u \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"$OUT/covered.txt\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\" > \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"$OUT/covered.sorted\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\\n   395\\\\\\\\tcomm -23 \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"$OUT/all.txt\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\" \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"$OUT/covered.sorted\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\" > \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"$OUT/ns-uncovered.txt\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\\n   396\\\\\\\\techo \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"all=$(wc -l < $OUT/all.txt) covered=$(wc -l < $OUT/covered.sorted) uncovered=$(wc -l < $OUT/ns-uncovered.txt)\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\" | tee -a \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"$OUT/summary.txt\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\\n   397\\\\\\\\trun_shard() {\\\\\\\\n   398\\\\\\\\t  s=$1; f=\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"$OUT/ns-$s.txt\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"; [ -s \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"$f\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\" ] || return 0\\\\\\\\n   399\\\\\\\\t  args=(); while read -r n; do args+=(-n \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"$n\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"); done < \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"$f\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\\n   400\\\\\\\\t  t0=$(date +%s); clojure -M:test -e :slow \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"${args[@]}\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\" >\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"$OUT/$s.log\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\" 2>&1; rc=$?\\\\\\\\n   401\\\\\\\\t  echo \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"$s rc=$rc secs=$(( $(date +%s)-t0 )) $(ts) $(grep -E \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"^Ran \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\" \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"$OUT/$s.log\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\" | tail -1)\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\" | tee -a \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"$OUT/summary.txt\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\\n   402\\\\\\\\t}\\\\\\\\n   403\\\\\\\\texport -f run_shard; export OUT; export -f ts\\\\\\\\n   404\\\\\\\\tprintf \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"%s\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\" $SUBS uncovered | xargs -P \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"$PAR\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\" -I{} bash -c \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"run_shard {}\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\\n   405\\\\\\\\techo \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"done $(ts)\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\" | tee -a \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"$OUT/summary.txt\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\\n   406\\\\\\\\t```\\\\\\\\n   407\\\\\\\\t\\\\\\\\n   408\\\\\\\\t**The slow tier** runs each tagged namespace on its own JVM, a few at a time:\\\\\\\\n   409\\\\\\\\t\\\\\\\\n   410\\\\\\\\t```sh\\\\\\\\n   411\\\\\\\\t#!/usr/bin/env bash\\\\\\\\n   412\\\\\\\\t# Usage: slow-tier.sh <clone> [parallel] -- the ^:slow tests of the tagged namespaces, one JVM per namespace\\\\\\\\n   413\\\\\\\\tset -u\\\\\\\\n   414\\\\\\\\texport PATH=\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"$HOME/.local/bin:/snap/bin:$PATH\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\\n   415\\\\\\\\tcd \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"$1\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\" || exit 2\\\\\\\\n   416\\\\\\\\tPAR=\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"${2:-6}\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\\n   417\\\\\\\\tmise trust >/dev/null 2>&1\\\\\\\\n   418\\\\\\\\teval \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"$(mise env -s bash)\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\\n   419\\\\\\\\tOUT=\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"$1/target-ci/slowtier\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"; rm -rf \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"$OUT\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"; mkdir -p \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"$OUT\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\\n   420\\\\\\\\trun_ns() {\\\\\\\\n   421\\\\\\\\t  n=$1; t0=$(date +%s)\\\\\\\\n   422\\\\\\\\t  clojure -M:test -i :slow -n \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"$n\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\" > \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"$OUT/$n.log\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\" 2>&1; rc=$?\\\\\\\\n   423\\\\\\\\t  echo \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"$n rc=$rc secs=$(( $(date +%s)-t0 )) $(grep -E \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"^Ran \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\" \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"$OUT/$n.log\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\" | tail -1)\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\" >> \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"$OUT/summary.txt\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\\n   424\\\\\\\\t}\\\\\\\\n   425\\\\\\\\texport -f run_ns; export OUT\\\\\\\\n   426\\\\\\\\techo \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"start $(date +%H:%M:%S) $(git rev-parse --short HEAD) par=$PAR\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\" > \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"$OUT/summary.txt\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\\n   427\\\\\\\\txargs -P \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"$PAR\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\" -I{} bash -c \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"run_ns {}\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\" < \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"$HOME/ci/pertest-ns.txt\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\\n   428\\\\\\\\techo \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"done $(date +%H:%M:%S)\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\" >> \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"$OUT/summary.txt\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\\n   429\\\\\\\\t```\\\\\\\\n   430\\\\\\\\t\\\\\\\\n   200\\\\\\\\t  the worktree). NOTE: the S1-era briefs and findings (1793294…-1793340…: the ownership map, the\\\\\\\\n   201\\\\\\\\t  inventory findings, the S1/S3 briefs, the pins/resume/expectations rounds, the S1 gate) were\\\\\\\\n   202\\\\\\\\t  absent from collab/ at archive time — likely swept by an interim bulk pass; their substance lives\\\\\\\\n   203\\\\\\\\t  in this log, the landed commits, and the gate artifacts that survived. collab/ is now empty.\\\\\\\\n   204\\\\\\\\tThe final handoff: the yang.python seat's 8.10 integration is DONE; the next seat (or this one, on\\\\\\\\n   205\\\\\\\\t  return) owns the 8.10.11 conformance evidence (bidirectional/higher-order cross-language fixtures,\\\\\\\\n   206\\\\\\\\t  bundled/linked equivalence — the entry fixture is the base), the worker-isolation debt row, and\\\\\\\\n   207\\\\\\\\t  monitoring the nightly. The standing rules: the two-tier testing policy, the dao.stream merge\\\\\\\\n   208\\\\\\\\t  precondition, the laptop-unload rule, the shared-checkout staging rule (nobody's staging area),\\\\\\\\n   209\\\\\\\\t  the slow-bodies rule for slow-guarded surfaces. Prior session log: docs/orchestrator-log.md (the\\\\\\\\n   210\\\\\\\\t  pre-handoff era) + this file. The tree: origin/master at efc99cc4.\\\\\\\\n   211\\\\\\\\t## 2026-10-31 12:5x +07 — the nightly rescheduled to 3am VIETNAM time (the owner: shiva is in Philadelphia)\\\\\\\\n   212\\\\\\\\tThe owner's correction: shiva sits in Philadelphia (EDT), so the 3am crontab fired at shiva's local\\\\\\\\n   213\\\\\\\\t  3am — the wrong window (it would also drift an hour when US DST ends). Reinstalled: the crontab\\\\\\\\n   214\\\\\\\\t  now fires HOURLY and ~/ci/nightly-full.sh carries a guard that runs the suite only when\\\\\\\\n   215\\\\\\\\t  TZ=Asia/Ho_Chi_Minh date +%H == 03 — the run always lands in the Vietnam 3am hour, immune to US\\\\\\\\n   216\\\\\\\\t  DST shifts forever. The first run: tonight at 03:00 ICT (in ~14 hours from this entry; the\\\\\\\\n   217\\\\\\\\t  previous 3am-EDT window had not fired yet, so no nightly has run at all — debut tonight). The\\\\\\\\n   218\\\\\\\\t  cron log: ~/ci/nightly-cron.log; per-stamp summaries: ~/ci/nightly-results/. Cost of the\\\\\\\\n   219\\\\\\\\t  DST-proof form: the script is invoked 24x/day and exits in ~1s for 23 of them.\\\\\\\\n   220\\\\\\\\t\\\\\\\\n   221\\\\\\\\t## 2026-10-31 03:3x +07 — the nightly is now MULTI-CORE (the owner caught the single-core problem)\\\\\\\\n   222\\\\\\\\tOwner, verbatim: \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"it doesn't look like the tests are utilizing multiple cores\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\" — confirmed: both\\\\\\\\n   223\\\\\\\\t  hosts ran the monolithic clojure -M:test at ~114% CPU (one core; load ~1.8 on 24/48 cores, the\\\\\\\\n   224\\\\\\\\t  ma