\\\\n   132\\\\t    ;; R1: the bundle's own inventory is the authority on what can run\\\\n   133\\\\t    (let [{:keys [out]} (psh {:dir clone :out :string :continue true}\\\\n   134\\\\t                             \\\\\\\"node\\\\\\\" \\\\\\\"target/node-tests.js\\\\\\\" \\\\\\\"--list\\\\\\\")\\\\n   135\\\\t          bundle (->> (str/split-lines out)\\\\n   136\\\\t                      (keep #(re-find #\\\\\\\"^Namespace: (\\\\\\\\S+)\\\\\\\" %))\\\\n   137\\\\t                      (map second)\\\\n   138\\\\t                      set)\\\\n   139\\\\t          lists (into {}\\\\n   140\\\\t                      (map (fn [s]\\\\n   141\\\\t                             [s (some->> (str out \\\\\\\"/ns-\\\\\\\" s \\\\\\\".txt\\\\\\\")\\\\n   142\\\\t                                         slurp\\\\n   143\\\\t                                         str/split-lines\\\\n   144\\\\t                                         (remove str/blank?)\\\\n   145\\\\t                                         vec)])\\\\n   146\\\\t                           subs))\\\\n   147\\\\t          lists (cond-> lists\\\\n   148\\\\t                  (.exists (fs/file (str out \\\\\\\"/ns-uncovered.txt\\\\\\\")))\\\\n   149\\\\t                  (assoc \\\\\\\"uncovered\\\\\\\"\\\\n   150\\\\t                         (->> (slurp (str out \\\\\\\"/ns-uncovered.txt\\\\\\\"))\\\\n   151\\\\t                              str/split-lines\\\\n   152\\\\t                              (remove str/blank?)\\\\n   153\\\\t                              vec)))\\\\n   154\\\\t          sel (into {} (map (fn [[s nss]] [s (filterv bundle nss)])) lists)\\\\n   155\\\\t          missing (into {}\\\\n   156\\\\t                        (remove (fn [[_ nss]] (empty? nss)))\\\\n   157\\\\t                        (into {}\\\\n   158\\\\t                              (map (fn [[s nss]]\\\\n   159\\\\t                                     [s (set/difference (set nss) bundle)]))\\\\n   160\\\\t                              lists))]\\\\n   161\\\\t      (doseq [[s miss] missing]\\\\n   162\\\\t        (fail! (str \\\\\\\"shard \\\\\\\" s \\\\\\\" requests namespaces absent from the compiled bundle: \\\\\\\"\\\\n   163\\\\t                    (str/join \\\\\\\",\\\\\\\" miss))))\\\\n   164\\\\t      ;; run up to PAR shards at a time (waves)\\\\n   165\\\\t      (let [t0 (System/currentTimeMillis)\\\\n   166\\\\t            shards (vec (filter (comp seq sel) (keys sel)))\\\\n   167\\\\t            runs (atom {})\\\\n   168\\\\t            run-one (fn [s]\\\\n   169\\\\t                      (let [t0 (System/currentTimeMillis)\\\\n   170\\\\t                            {:keys [exit]}\\\\n   171\\\\t                            (psh {:dir clone\\\\n   172\\\\t                                  :out (str out \\\\\\\"/\\\\\\\" s \\\\\\\".log\\\\\\\")\\\\n   173\\\\t                                  :err :append\\\\n   174\\\\t                                  :extra-env {\\\\\\\"DATOM_SLOW_TESTS\\\\\\\" \\\\\\\"1\\\\\\\"}\\\\n   175\\\\t                                  :continue true}\\\\n   176\\\\t                                 \\\\\\\"node\\\\\\\" \\\\\\\"target/node-tests.js\\\\\\\"\\\\n   177\\\\t                                 \\\\\\\"--test\\\\\\\" (str/join \\\\\\\",\\\\\\\" (sel s)))\\\\n   178\\\\t                            secs (quot (- (System/currentTimeMillis) t0) 1000)]\\\\n   179\\\\t                        (swap! runs assoc s {:rc exit :secs secs})\\\\n   180\\\\t                        (spit (str out \\\\\\\"/runs.txt\\\\\\\")\\\\n   181\\\\t                              (str s \\\\\\\" rc=\\\\\\\" exit \\\\\\\" secs=\\\\\\\" secs \\\\\\\"\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\")\\\\n   182\\\\t                              :append true)))]\\\\n   183\\\\t        (doseq [batch (partition-all par shards)]\\\\n   184\\\\t          (->> batch\\\\n   185\\\\t               (mapv (fn [s] (future (run-one s))))\\\\n   186\\\\t               (mapv deref)))\\\\n   187\\\\t        (let [expected (count shards)\\\\n   188\\\\t              done (count @runs)\\\\n   189\\\\t              red (count (filter #(not= 0 (:rc %)) (vals @runs)))\\\\n   190\\\\t              wall (quot (- (System/currentTimeMillis) t0) 1000)]\\\\n   191\\\\t          (doseq [[s r] (sort @runs)]\\\\n   192\\\\t            (log (str s \\\\\\\" rc=\\\\\\\" (:rc r) \\\\\\\" secs=\\\\\\\" (:secs r))))\\\\n   193\\\\t          (log (str \\\\\\\"node-sharded lanes=\\\\\\\" done \\\\\\\" red-lanes=\\\\\\\" red\\\\n   194\\\\t                    \\\\\\\" wall=\\\\\\\" wall \\\\\\\"s\\\\\\\"))\\\\n   195\\\\t          (when-not (= expected done)\\\\n   196\\\\t            (fail! (str \\\\\\\"expected \\\\\\\" expected \\\\\\\" shards, completed \\\\\\\" done)))\\\\n   197\\\\t          (when (pos? red)\\\\n   198\\\\t            (fail! (str red \\\\\\\" red shards\\\\\\\"))))))\\\\n   199\\\\t    (log (str \\\\\\\"done rc=\\\\\\\" @rc))\\\\n\\\",\\\"exit_code\\\":0,\\\"status\\\":\\\"completed\\\"}}\\n87:{\\\"type\\\":\\\"item.completed\\\",\\\"item\\\":{\\\"id\\\":\\\"item_44\\\",\\\"type\\\":\\\"agent_message\\\",\\\"text\\\":\\\"Reviewed `master@4d9a84a8094b3bc747a46afad7e48b3c765bbb8e` against my original findings. Shiva’s three Clojure driver files match this checkout byte for byte. I also inspected both deployed wrappers and Jupiter’s JVM runners. No suites were launched or files changed.\\\\n\\\\nSeveral claimed fixes are absent from this revision.\\\\n\\\\n**R1 — coverage and execution**\\\\n\\\\n- **“Run Dart’s residual” — STILL-OPEN.** The residual is now included in the emission loop at [dart_shard.clj:132](/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/src/dev/dart_shard.clj:132), which fixes the original loop omission. However, the driver cannot load: `io/writer` at line 81 has no namespace require. `bb -e '(load-file \\\\\\\"src/dev/dart_shard.clj\\\\\\\")'` reproduced `Unable to resolve symbol: io/writer`.\\\\n\\\\n  Further execution blockers remain:\\\\n  - Both namespace parsers merely drop the first output line, then consume indentation; neither seeks its lane header: [node_shard.clj:64](/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/src/dev/node_shard.clj:64), [dart_shard.clj:52](/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/src/dev/dart_shard.clj:52). Actual output starts with `Read …` and `Subsystems:`, before the lane sections ([affected.clj:751](/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/src/dev/affected.clj:751)). A successful actual `yang.base` listing reports six CLJS namespaces; feeding that output into the current Node parser returns `[]`.\\\\n  - Both disk scans convert absolute paths without first making them relative to the clone: [node_shard.clj:112](/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/src/dev/node_shard.clj:112), [dart_shard.clj:89](/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/src/dev/dart_shard.clj:89). For example, `/tmp/clone/test/yang/base/foo_test.cljc` becomes `.tmp.clone.test.yang.base.foo-test`.\\\\n  - Dart’s threaded `apply concat` at [dart_shard.clj:114](/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/src/dev/dart_shard.clj:114) splits subsystem namespace strings into characters. Its unconditional residual `slurp` also throws when no residual file exists.\\\\n\\\\n- **“Include JVM slow tests” — CLOSED at the wiring level.** `jupiter:~/ci/nightly-jvm.sh:67–79` now discovers namespaces and invokes `clojure -M:test -i :slow -n \\\\\\\"$n\\\\\\\"` alongside the quick tier. This closes the original complete absence of the slow-tier invocation. Full-tier execution remains unvalidated.\\\\n\\\\n- **“Rebuild required peers at the selected SHA” — STILL-OPEN.** Node now requests both builds at [node_shard.clj:104](/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/src/dev/node_shard.clj:104). Jupiter still builds only the Node peer: `~/ci/shard-jvm.sh:12–14`; its wrapper adds no Dart-peer build. Inspection found no `build/yin-repl-peer` in Jupiter’s nightly clone. The documented JVM skip condition therefore remains ([bb.edn:250](/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/bb.edn:250)).\\\\n\\\\n- **“Reconcile planned namespaces against fresh runtime/generated inventories, recording explicit lane exclusions” — STILL-OPEN.** The bundle’s `--list` **is authoritative for tests registered in that compiled bundle**: shadow-cljs 3.3.5’s `shadow/test/node.cljs:74–82` prints `env/get-tests`.\\\\n\\\\n  The pre-run check is not airtight:\\\\n  - At [node_shard.clj:133](/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/src/dev/node_shard.clj:133), destructured process stdout named `out` shadows the output-directory binding. Subsequent `slurp` paths use the inventory text as their directory.\\\\n  - The inventory command’s exit status is ignored.\\\\n  - Only `requested − bundle` is checked; runnable bundle namespaces absent from the plan are not reconciled.\\\\n  - Legitimate lane exclusions are not recorded.\\\\n\\\\n- **“Fail on unexplained missing execution” — STILL-OPEN.** Unknown requested namespaces do set the aggregate failure flag at [node_shard.clj:161](/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/src/dev/node_shard.clj:161), but execution has another independent defect: line 177 passes `\\\\\\\"--test\\\\\\\"` and the namespace list separately. Shadow 3.3.5 accepts only `--test=…` (`shadow/test/node.cljs:30–39`). With no recognized selector, it runs **all tests** (`:88–89`). After the preceding blockers are fixed, each supposed shard would therefore run the full bundle unless this argument is corrected.\\\\n\\\\n**R3 — Flutter writable state**\\\\n\\\\n- **“Use isolated project copies, or one Flutter invocation over all emitted files with a single concurrency budget” — CLOSED for the cache-isolation mechanism.** [dart_shard.clj:153](/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/src/dev/dart_shard.clj:153) constructs one invocation over all collected directories, with one concurrency argument.\\\\n\\\\n  Shiva’s installed Flutter 3.47.1 `packages/flutter_tools/lib/src/test/test_compiler.dart:90–94` explicitly serializes compilation requests. Lines 112–129 select the shared cache; lines 277–291 update it. Multiple test workers inside this invocation do not recreate the original competing Flutter-command writers. Exclusive ownership of the clone remains necessary.\\\\n\\\\n- **“Treat emission failures as fatal” — CLOSED for result propagation.** At [dart_shard.clj:144](/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/src/dev/dart_shard.clj:144), failed emissions set `rc=1` and their directories are excluded from the invocation. Successful directories may still run, but the aggregate cannot finish green through that branch.\\\\n\\\\n- **“Use fresh, run-specific output directories” — STILL-OPEN.** Both output and aggregator names have only minute precision: [dart_shard.clj:64](/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/src/dev/dart_shard.clj:64), line 136. A same-minute rerun reuses the directory; `write-shards!` deletes the existing aggregator tree ([cljd_agg.clj:151](/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/src/dev/cljd_agg.clj:151)). There is no lock or exclusive directory creation.\\\\n\\\\n**R4 — pin protocol**\\\\n\\\\n- **“Atomically publish `{run-id, full-SHA, timestamp}`” — CLOSED for a single publisher.** `shiva:~/ci/nightly-full.sh:28–31` writes the requested fields and renames a temporary file in the same directory. Concurrent publishers remain unsafe because they share `nightly-pin.tmp` and have no lock.\\\\n\\\\n- **“Require the expected Vietnam nightly date” — CLOSED.** `jupiter:~/ci/nightly-jvm.sh:27,41–43` compares the pin date with Vietnam’s current date. Yesterday’s pin can no longer be accepted as pinned.\\\\n\\\\n  However, lines 35–36 stop polling upon seeing **any** `run-id=` record, including yesterday’s. Starting just before publication therefore causes immediate advisory fallback instead of waiting for today’s pin.\\\\n\\\\n- **“Validate the commit” — STILL-OPEN.** Lines 44–45 add the requested refetch retry, but `git cat-file -e \\\\\\\"$PSHA\\\\\\\"` checks object existence, not commit type, and the parser does not require a full-length SHA.\\\\n\\\\n- **“Check every Git command and actual HEAD” — STILL-OPEN.** Shiva checks fetch and checkout, but not SHA resolution/publication. Jupiter leaves fallback checkout unchecked at line 50 and never verifies actual `HEAD` against the chosen full SHA. Its initial fetch failure is logged through `fail`, then that diagnostic is overwritten by line 55.\\\\n\\\\n- **“Join results only by matching run-id and SHA” — STILL-OPEN.** Jupiter’s line 41 parses `20261101-0300` as just `20261101`; I reproduced this. The generation suffix is lost. A prior same-day run can be accepted, and summaries do not consistently carry the complete run ID and full SHA for reconciliation.\\\\n\\\\n- **“Record fallback reasons explicitly” — STILL-OPEN.** The advisory label and `RC=1` are present at lines 49–52. However, the single reason string `absent/stale/unreachable` does not identify the actual cause and also covers object-validation or checkout failures.\\\\n\\\\n**R6 — evidence integrity**\\\\n\\\\n- **“Preserve immutable per-run plans, prerequisite logs, emission logs, shard stdout/stderr, and result records” — STILL-OPEN.** The new directory layout improves retention, but minute collisions allow reuse and appending: [node_shard.clj:76](/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/src/dev/node_shard.clj:76), [dart_shard.clj:64](/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/src/dev/dart_shard.clj:64). The summaries lack consistent full-SHA/run-ID/host/toolchain manifests.\\\\n\\\\n  Jupiter copies quick-tier evidence after completion (`nightly-jvm.sh:64–65`), but `shard-jvm.sh:9` still deletes its fixed evidence directory before each run. Evidence from an interrupted run can disappear before being copied.\\\\n\\\\n- **“Aggregate against the expected shard set” — STILL-OPEN.** Node compares completed count with a count derived from its already-filtered selection: [node_shard.clj:166](/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/src/dev/node_shard.clj:166), lines 187–196. An empty selection produces expected=completed=0. This does not establish completeness against an independently preserved plan. Dart has no emitted/executed set reconciliation. Jupiter’s quick tier counts existing result rows without comparing them against expected shards.\\\\n\\\\n- **“Return nonzero for failed, missing, or incomplete work” — STILL-OPEN across the nightly.** The Node/Dart aggregate exit paths and Shiva’s wrapper now propagate recorded failures. Jupiter still ignores the quick-runner exit status (`nightly-jvm.sh:59–63`); zero result rows yield zero red rows and can be accepted. Slow-tier count checking is an improvement, but does not repair quick-tier accounting.\\\\n\\\\n- **“Distinguish incomplete infrastructure from test failures” — STILL-OPEN.** Infrastructure and test failures share an undifferentiated aggregate result, and uncaught driver errors bypass completion records.\\\\n\\\\n- **“Sync matching manifests with bounded timeouts, keeping local evidence authoritative” — STILL-OPEN.** Both wrappers create the destination directory and retain local summaries. However, `ConnectTimeout` is applied to the preceding `ssh`, **not** the `scp` (`shiva:48–50`, `jupiter:82–84`). Neither operation has a total duration bound, and the transferred summaries lack the matching manifests required above.\\\\n\\\\nThe timestamp substitution does not match the description: the drivers put `stamp` in the initial line and directory name; their logging functions do not timestamp each summary line ([node_shard.clj:85](/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/src/dev/node_shard.clj:85), [dart_shard.clj:73](/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/src/dev/dart_shard.clj:73)). A run timestamp plus elapsed durations could suffice; restoring shell `ts` is not itself a blocker. Unique identity, provenance, and completion evidence remain blockers.\\\\n\\\\n**Additional fixes checked**\\\\n\\\\n- **`:extra-env` preserves HOME — confirmed.** A focused probe preserved HOME. Node’s helper also merges caller additions correctly.\\\\n- **Dart drops its slow-test setting.** [dart_shard.clj:44](/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/src/dev/dart_shard.clj:44) replaces caller `:extra-env` with PATH alone, discarding `DATOM_SLOW_TESTS=1` supplied at line 156.\\\\n- **`:err :append` remains in execution paths:** Node line 173; Dart lines 140 and 155. On both local Babashka and Shiva, a harmless `/bin/echo` succeeded with `:err :string` and failed with `:err :append`, reporting ENOENT. The prerequisite redirections were corrected; these calls were not.\\\\n- **`mise exec -- npm ci` is correctly wired** at [node_shard.clj:100](/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/src/dev/node_shard.clj:100). The earlier PATH-only environment replacement is fixed.\\\\n- **The aggregator flags are implemented:** [cljd_agg.clj:175](/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/src/dev/cljd_agg.clj:175), lines 189 and 208–218 preserve the default compile/run path while supporting emission-only operation.\\\\n\\\\nThe reported 10/14 green shards remain partial evidence from an earlier implementation. They do not validate these current execution paths. The original R2 full parallel validation and clone-exclusivity concerns remain outstanding.\\\\n\\\\n**OVERALL: STILL-REVISE.** The Flutter cache fix, slow-tier wiring, and previous-date pin rejection close real issues. The current deployed drivers still contain reproducible startup and execution defects, and the nightly can still accept incomplete JVM work.\\\"}}\\n\",\"exit_code\":0,\"status\":\"completed\"}}\ncollab/dao-stream/1789630001089-architect-dao-stream-v1-retirement-plan.claude-fable-5-1.raw.json:1:{\"duration_api_ms\":702321,\"stop_reason\":\"end_turn\",\"session_id\":\"a4aea5af-4571-4db4-b3a3-b4ffa5b641b5\",\"total_cost_usd\":8.266223749999998,\"usage\":{\"input_tokens\":386,\"cache_creation_input_tokens\":245069,\"cache_read_input_tokens\":1829407,\"output_tokens\":58013,\"output_tokens_details\":{\"thinking_tokens\":14180},\"server_tool_use\":{\"web_search_requests\":0,\"web_fetch_requests\":0},\"service_tier\":\"standard\",\"cache_creation\":{\"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens