0p;1445,1461p'\\\"\",\"aggregated_output\":\"  1202\\t**Lift** (emitter side; composition-driven, never automatic on every park):\\n  1203\\t\\n  1204\\t1. The machine is parked or blocked with a local record `r`, and its\\n  1205\\t   ready-queue is empty, else `:yin.k/not-quiescent`.\\n  1206\\t2. **Enter exporting** (§7.7.4): detach the wait set into the export\\n  1207\\t   record, neutralize direct `:resume`. From here the source is fenced; no\\n  1208\\t   poll, retry, or local resume can perform an effect.\\n  1209\\t3. `lift(export-record)`: confirm the record is at a safepoint (§7.4.1),\\n  1210\\t   else `:yin.k/not-at-safepoint`; canonicalize every referenced segment and\\n  1211\\t   compute its address (§7.3.2), else the refusal; encode (§7.5), else the\\n  1212\\t   refusal; compute `:yin.k/requires` and `:yin.k/store` by the fixed point\\n  1213\\t   (§7.6), recording the discovery status; stamp the contract (§7.3.3); on\\n  1214\\t   first export, mint the occurrence; mint `:yin.k/id`.\\n  1215\\t4. Append the canonical instruction vectors of every required segment to a\\n  1216\\t   `dao.jing` intake pool (the payloads *are* the vectors, §7.3.4), then\\n  1217\\t   the id-less value body to the carrier medium; observe `:dao.stream/ok`\\n  1218\\t   on each. `:yin.k/carried` may then be empty. Retry of any failed append\\n  1219\\t   reuses the occurrence (§7.7.4).\\n  1220\\t5. Under `:exclusive`, append `:yin.k/offered` to the arbitration medium.\\n  1221\\t   The export record stays for recovery; the emitter is now a candidate\\n  1222\\t   like any other, and wakes only on custody (a grant to itself), never on\\n  1223\\t   data.\\n  1224\\t\\n  1225\\t**Lower** (resumer side):\\n  1226\\t\\n  1227\\t1. Read the value; check `:yin.k/contract`, else `:yin.k/profile-mismatch`.\\n  1228\\t2. Verify `:yin.k/id` by re-hashing the body, else `:yin.k/hash-mismatch`.\\n  1229\\t3. Decode against the §7.5.1 grammar with full structural validation, else\\n  1230\\t   `:yin.k/undecodable` — a correct hash is not structural validation, and\\n  1231\\t   both checks always run.\\n  1232\\t4. Evaluate `:yin.k/requires` (§7.6.5); fetch what may be fetched (segments\\n  1233\\t   by address, verified by re-canonicalization); else\\n  1234\\t   `:yin.k/unsatisfied` with the discovery status.\\n  1235\\t5. Under `:exclusive`, attach to the arbitration medium (an attachment\\n  1236\\t   failure here is `:yin.k/unsatisfied` naming it — the value declares its\\n  1237\\t   authority, §7.7.3), propose, then observe the grant, else\\n  1238\\t   `:yin.k/not-holder` with the lease state observed; while a proposal is\\n  1239\\t   unanswered the driver's step answers `:yin.k/awaiting-grant` — a\\n  1240\\t   grantor owes no answer and no bound applies (`dao.lease.md`,\\n  1241\\t   *Authority*).\\n  1242\\t6. Load every required segment by address into the per-stamp index,\\n  1243\\t   verifying each (§7.3.4).\\n  1244\\t7. **Restore into an isolated store** (§7.6.2): the slice, the remapped\\n  1245\\t   cells, the resumer's FFI pair. Attach to every stream descriptor in the\\n  1246\\t   frame, pending waits, and cells (§7.4.3); an attachment `not-found` is\\n  1247\\t   `:yin.k/unsatisfied` naming the stream. **Any failure from this step\\n  1248\\t   onward — after custody was acquired — releases first**: the resumer\\n  1249\\t   appends `:dao.lease/released`, the occurrence returns to offered, and\\n  1250\\t   the failure outcome is returned. A resumer that dies without releasing\\n  1251\\t   is recovered by the lease's own lapse; nothing else is owed.\\n  1252\\t8. `lower(frame, layout)` into engine registers; re-mint every pending wait\\n  1253\\t   in the local wait set; seed `:id-counter` per §7.6.3; run — through a\\n  1254\\t   fenced writer under `:exclusive` (§7.7.5).\\n  1255\\t9. At the next safepoint or halt, produce the successor occurrence\\n  1322\\t  its wiring becomes the worked example. A composition without a\\n  1323\\t  transactable space offers `:yin.k/fork` only.\\n  1324\\t- **Execution identity.** Occurrence minting, the `:yin.k/origin` chain,\\n  1325\\t  retry idempotence (one occurrence per park), and successor completion as\\n  1326\\t  a grantor ledger transition need conformance tests, including the crash\\n  1327\\t  windows of §7.7.5.\\n  1328\\t- **Pending-state completeness.** Every pending variant of §7.4.3 must\\n  1329\\t  round-trip and resume *elsewhere*: retained writes, sent and retained FFI\\n  1330\\t  calls with both endpoints and the kept response cursor, and cursor cells\\n  1331\\t  through the aliasing scenarios of `check-wait-set`. This depends on a\\n  1332\\t  generated stream-over-network facade and a **portable cursor profile**\\n  1333\\t  that preserves the source stream's kept cursor and `gap` outcomes. The\\n  1334\\t  M4 string-backed stream test below is the required cross-host proof.\\n  1335\\t- **Enforceable fencing.** Epoch-checked, atomic-with-commitment admission\\n  1336\\t  and durable op-id plus intent dedup at enrolled consumers are design\\n  1337\\t  items for `dao.space.transactor.md`. A consumer without a shared atomic\\n  1338\\t  boundary declares at-least-once or fail-stop behavior; it cannot claim\\n  1339\\t  exactly-once custody from the lease alone.\\n  1340\\t- **Canonical byte encoding.** `:yin.code/hash` and `:yin.k/id` are exactly\\n  1445\\t  static kind alone.\\n  1446\\t  Test both FFI states and each call effect. `lift(lower(frame))` must\\n  1447\\t  reproduce the canonical frame. An undeclared pc gives\\n  1448\\t  `:yin.k/not-at-safepoint`; queued work gives `:yin.k/not-quiescent`.\\n  1449\\t  Insufficient pending evidence refuses before publication, as does a\\n  1450\\t  missing portable cursor profile. Halt yields a result, not a frame.\\n  1451\\t- Facade acceptance: Park a continuation holding a string-backed local\\n  1452\\t  `dao.stream` with a kept cursor, then migrate to another network node.\\n  1453\\t  The exporter mechanically serves that stream through the standard\\n  1454\\t  facade; the cell descriptor contains the facade endpoint and kept\\n  1455\\t  cursor, and the receiver binds a proxy `dao.stream` to the original\\n  1456\\t  logical stream. Reads resume at the kept position. Force retention\\n  1457\\t  loss and verify the proxy returns `:dao.stream/gap` with the source's\\n  1458\\t  successor cursor, without replay or silent skip. Repeat with a source\\n  1459\\t  that cannot honor the profile: lift refuses `:yin.k/unsatisfied`; an\\n  1460\\t  unreachable endpoint on lower is `:yin.k/unsatisfied` naming the stream.\\n  1461\\t- Landing and order: M4 covers the early two-engine gate, the table,\\n\",\"exit_code\":0,\"status\":\"completed\"}}\ncollab/dao-stream/1790865064522-cljd-reader-bugs-upstream-report.md:128:Severity: medium. We compare macro expansions across hosts in our\ncollab/dao-stream/architect-phase5-r3-r4-cleanup-fixes-verification-r4.fable.prompt.md:39:  failed on two unchanged baseline reader-conditionals in\ncollab/dao-stream/architect-phase5-r3-r4-cleanup-fixes-verification-r4.fable.prompt.md:51:findings, any effect of the noted baseline CLJD test compile failure on this\ncollab/dao-stream/1792455434000-architect-stream-codec-design.claude-fable-5-1.findings.md:33:C0 contract namespace and base domain, Transit keeps forwarding vars (astra A2), law test over both profiles. C1 `dao.stream.ws` without Transit require or defaults, key rename, parameterized codec fixture, `dao.stream.ws.md` sentence amended. C2 `dao.jing.stream` by capability, with nil/empty/unknown/valid tests (astra A3). C3 host adapters. C4 `remote-channel` and yin.repl name their codec. C5 owner-gated CBOR default. Each: three lanes green, counts recorded, cross-host peer suites unchanged. J6 depends on C0-C4; nothing else in the jolt plan does.\ncollab/dao-stream/1790502148751-vm-engineer-dao-stream-remote-slice6.claude.findings.md:13:- JVM: `clj -M:test` → 2276 tests / 183262 assertions / 0 failures, 0 errors (baseline 2254/183121/0 plus other in-flight sessions' own added tests plus mine; no failures anywhere, `dao.stream.udp-test` included and green).\ncollab/dao-stream/1790485743084-vm-engineer-dao-stream-remote-slice3-r2.glm-flash.report.md:27:- Node `bb test:cljs`: **2,177 tests / 49,865 assertions / 0 failures, 0 errors** (baseline 2,167/49,829 → +10/+36 = my portable namespace).\ncollab/dao-stream/1790485743084-vm-engineer-dao-stream-remote-slice3-r2.glm-flash.report.md:28:- Dart `bb test:cljd`: **2,139 passed, all tests passed** (baseline 2,129 → +10).\ncollab/dao-stream/1790485743084-vm-engineer-dao-stream-remote-slice3-r2.glm-flash.report.md:31:The true cross-host socket proofs, which need a remote-protocol peer program per host (the `dao.stream.slice-peer` pattern): compose these same `dao.stream.ws-project` acceptor/dial pieces with `dao.stream.ws.node` and `dao.stream.ws.dart` in a peer namespace, then run **clj→Node** (clj listener serves, Node dials and reads), **Node→clj** (Node's acceptor serves, clj's dial reflects back over the same connection), and **cljd→clj** (clj serves, the Dart peer dials). The namespace is portable and already compiles/runs on the Node and Dart lanes (unit tests above). The browser dials-and-reads lane is also yours: no browser harness exists in the three lanes; the composition is identical with `dao.stream.ws.browser/connect!` as the dial side.\ncollab/dao-stream/1790476870000-vm-engineer-dao-stream-remote-slice2-fixes.glm-flash.report.md:20:- JVM `mise exec -- clojure -M:test`: Ran 2,254 tests containing 183,208 assertions. 0 failures, 0 errors. (baseline 2,252/183,193/0; +2/+15)\ncollab/dao-stream/1790476870000-vm-engineer-dao-stream-remote-slice2-fixes.glm-flash.report.md:21:- Node `mise exec -- bb test:cljs`: Ran 2,166 tests containing 49,814 assertions. 0 failures, 0 errors. (baseline 2,164/49,799/0; +2/+15)\ncollab/dao-stream/1790476870000-vm-engineer-dao-stream-remote-slice2-fixes.glm-flash.report.md:22:- Dart `mise exec -- bb test:cljd`: All tests passed! — 2,128 passed. (baseline 2,126; +2; new tests verified present in the fresh `test/cljd-out/dao/stream/remote-test_test.dart`)\ncollab/dao-stream/1790969350000-orchestrator-c2s2-cljd.log:1718:04:19 +1157: /Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-py-c2gen1/test/cljd-out/yin/vm/debruijn-code-test_test.dart: null yin.vm.debruijn-code-test/identical-bytes-across-hosts-for-common-domain\ncollab/dao-stream/1792482520000-engineer-codec-f0-fixes.claude-sonnet-5-5.findings.md:6:## P1: baseline incompatibilities preserved as exception evidence\ncollab/dao-stream/1792482520000-engineer-codec-f0-fixes.claude-sonnet-5-5.findings.md:10:New deftest `frozen-baseline-exceptions-keep-their-per-host-outcome` asserts the recorded outcome on the running host. The envelopes.edn corpora are unchanged. The reviewer's request for an architect-approved scope amendment is still open: this records the evidence, it does not grant the amendment.\ncollab/dao-stream/1790536094287-architect-dao-stream-remote-slice8-confirm-r3.gpt-6-sol.stdout.log:12:{\"type\":\"item.completed\",\"item\":{\"id\":\"item_5\",\"type\":\"command_execution\",\"command\":\"/bin/zsh -lc 'cat collab/1790530102473-architect-dao-stream-remote-slice8-confirm.gpt-6-sol.stdout.log'\",\"aggregated_output\":\"{\\\"type\\\":\\\"thread.started\\\",\\\"thread_id\\\":\\\"01a0e3e9-2743-7a23-b06b-0b0b1e9e2af4\\\"}\\n{\\\"type\\\":\\\"turn.started\\\"}\\n{\\\"type\\\":\\\"item.completed\\\",\\\"item\\\":{\\\"id\\\":\\\"item_0\\\",\\\"type\\\":\\\"agent_message\\\",\\\"text\\\":\\\"I’ll review the two slice-8 files against the engine’s parked state and the architecture rules, then check the lift/lower and codec seams. I’ll use the supplied test results and won’t rerun suites or edit files.\\\"}}\\n{\\\"type\\\":\\\"item.started\\\",\\\"item\\\":{\\\"id\\\":\\\"item_1\\\",\\\"type\\\":\\\"command_execution\\\",\\\"command\\\":\\\"/bin/zsh -lc 'cat docs/design/datom.world.md'\\\",\\\"aggregated_output\\\":\\\"\\\",\\\"exit_code\\\":null,\\\"status\\\":\\\"in_progress\\\"}}\\n{\\\"type\\\":\\\"item.completed\\\",\\\"item\\\":{\\\"id\\\":\\\"item_1\\\",\\\"type\\\":\\\"command_execution\\\",\\\"command\\\":\\\"/bin/zsh -lc 'cat docs/design/datom.world.md'\\\",\\\"aggregated_output\\\":\\\"---\\\\ndescription: Core philosophy, foundational axioms, invariants, primitives (tuples, streams, host boundaries), architectural commitments, design principles, code style, and development workflow for datom.world\\\\n---\\\\n\\\\n# DATOM.WORLD ARCHITECTURAL FOUNDATIONS & DEVELOPMENT RULES\\\\n\\\\n## Core Philosophy\\\\n\\\\nEverything is data.\\\\nInterpretation > abstraction.\\\\nExplicit causality > implicit assumptions.\\\\nRestrictions are a feature.\\\\n\\\\n### Foundational Axioms\\\\n\\\\n1. **Everything is a Stream**: All IO and data flow through append-only streams.\\\\n2. **Interpretation Creates Semantics**: Data is syntax; semantics only emerge through interpretation (one truth, many perspectives).\\\\n   At system scale, a \\\\\\\"system\\\\\\\" is an emergent property of interpreters of\\\\n   pure data, not an object, service, or stored artifact. Find the\\\\n   interpreters and the data they share to find the system.\\\\n3. **Code and State are Datoms**: Code (Universal AST) and runtime execution state are structured datoms, enabling syntax independence and structural reflection.\\\\n4. **Everything is a Continuation**: Computation is modeled as serializable, portable continuations that can pause, travel across streams, and resume anywhere.\\\\n\\\\n## Non-Negotiable Invariants\\\\n\\\\n- Do not introduce hidden global state.\\\\n- Do not introduce implicit control flow.\\\\n- Do not introduce callbacks; every callback is an event on a stream.\\\\n- Do not introduce shared mutable state.\\\\n- Do not collapse interpretation and execution into the same layer.\\\\n- Do not assume graphs: graphs must be constructed explicitly from tuples.\\\\n\\\\n## Tuples and Datoms\\\\n\\\\nTuples are elements in an open moduli space, graded by dimension $n$. A tuple can be any dimension/size.\\\\nA datom is the canonical persistent tuple `[e a v t m]` (entity, attribute, value, transaction, metadata). Persistent facts are immutable datoms.\\\\nSource scope belongs to the interpreter, never to an appended tuple slot. Queries keep physical sources as separate db-values and express union or joins explicitly.\\\\n\\\\nSee [`docs/design/datom.md`](./datom.md) for full specification.\\\\n\\\\n## Streams\\\\n\\\\nAll IO is modeled as a stream. Functions consume streams and produce streams.\\\\nNo direct function-to-function coupling without a stream boundary.\\\\nSide effects must appear as stream emissions.\\\\nStreams are values that can be sent through streams.\\\\nStreams carry whatever values the consumer needs: no datom requirement, no privileged payload shape.\\\\n\\\\nA stream has no privileged reader, and its meaning is not in it. Any number\\\\nof interpreters may observe the same medium, and each constructs its own\\\\nsemantics from the same batches: a `yin.vm` evaluator observing a program\\\\nstream constructs CESK state and executes it; `dao.space.index` observing\\\\nthe very same stream materializes covered indexes, so `dao.space.query/q`\\\\nanswers Datalog over the program as it grows. Neither knows the other\\\\nexists. The medium is their only coupling, and each observer's ignorance of\\\\nthe other is load-bearing: the evaluator never consults an index to run,\\\\nand the index never evaluates a form to index it. This is how axiom 2\\\\nbecomes architecture: one stream, many interpretations, none of them\\\\nthe stream's own.\\\\n\\\\nFunctions can take anything and return anything.\\\\nAgents are functions, closures, or continuations in `yin.vm` that communicate with the outside world through `dao.stream`. Agent behavior is specified entirely through stream effects.\\\\n\\\\nSee [`docs/design/dao.stream.md`](./dao.stream.md) for full stream specification.\\\\nSee [`docs/design/yin.vm.streams-all-the-way-down.md`](./yin.vm.streams-all-the-way-down.md) for VM architecture.\\\\n\\\\n### Host Boundaries\\\\n\\\\nA host boundary is a stream boundary, never a function call. The one\\\\nsanctioned function-shaped contact is a `dao.stream` handle operation, whose\\\\nexhaustive outcome map is stream protocol, not an application callback.\\\\n\\\\n**Effects out.** Portable code appends an effect value describing what must\\\\nhappen. A host interpreter consumes that stream, performs the operation, and\\\\nappends the outcome. Portable code reads the outcome. Correlation is by\\\\nidentity in the data; neither side holds a reference to the other. A host with\\\\nno implementation for an effect emits a qualified unsupported result. That is a\\\\ncorrect outcome, not a gap to be filled.\\\\n\\\\n**Events in.** When the host initiates (a socket receives, a connection drops,\\\\na timer fires) the adapter appends one plain-data event and returns. It invokes\\\\nnothing. An interpreter reads that stream and decides what the event means.\\\\nConstructively: **a callback is replaced by a function that transforms an event\\\\nto data on a stream.** The host's demand for a callback stops at that function.\\\\n\\\\n**Adapters.** An adapter is a map of those transform functions. That is all an\\\\nadapter is. It is a value, not a namespace, and it is general: sockets, files,\\\\ntimers and windows all deliver events by calling something, and an adapter is\\\\nwhat they call. Each entry takes the host's arguments and returns one value;\\\\nthe append is the adapter's, not the entry's, so an entry cannot return a value\\\\nto the host and cannot invoke application code. The adapter is handed only the\\\\ndeposit operation and its own host resource. If its deposit channel fails, it\\\\nmay close that resource to make the boundary observably gone; this is teardown,\\\\nnot an upward callback.\\\\n\\\\nHost types are classified into plain data in the transform: it is the last\\\\nplace holding a host error object, and no host type crosses onto the stream. A\\\\ntransport may use a qualified envelope to preserve correlation, lifecycle, and\\\\nadditive evolution; that envelope remains plain data and creates no separate\\\\nevent mechanism. A composition may likewise define its own qualified vocabulary\\\\nfor facts it owns.\\\\n\\\\nWhich stream an adapter writes to is the caller's composition, never the\\\\nadapter's knowledge. An adapter cannot tell whether it deposits into one\\\\ntransport's private stream or into a medium many interpreters read. This keeps\\\\nthe layering one-way: a boundary depends on nothing above it, because whoever\\\\nconstructs the adapter supplies the stream.\\\\n\\\\nA transform deposits every event admitted by the boundary protocol and judges\\\\nnone of them semantically. Wire framing, decoding, and protocol validation\\\\nhappen below the transform: malformed wire input is transport machinery, not an\\\\nevent. Once the transport has produced a valid host event, data is syntax\\\\n(axiom 2): an event that is noise to one interpreter is signal to another that\\\\ndoes not exist yet, and filtering at the depositing layer destroys perspectives\\\\nnot yet taken. Retention is the medium's operational policy; meaning is\\\\ninterpretation. Neither is the depositor's decision.\\\\n\\\\nTwo things are not adapters. One that exposes a function for portable code to\\\\ncall isolates the host library but keeps the coupling, and the effect never\\\\nappears as an emission. One that takes a function to invoke has relocated the\\\\ncallback, not removed it, even when every value it passes is plain data; if\\\\nthat callback has a meaningful return value, it is a synchronous call in both\\\\ndirections wearing the shape of an event.\\\\n\\\\n## Architectural Commitments\\\\n\\\\n- **`dao.jing` is syntax, agents are semantics**: the content-addressed encoding stays passive and payload-agnostic.\\\\n- **Macros are stream topology**: an evaluator knows nothing about macro expansion; expansion happens on the syntax side of a medium boundary, upstream of any evaluator.\\\\n- **Peer observers, one stream**: a generic evaluator and `dao.space` independently observe the same stream topic, as described under Streams. This is not a claim about any two consumers regardless of what they consume.\\\\n- **Observers are independent and optional**: nothing requires a medium to have any particular set of consumers. Which observers exist for a stream is a per-composition choice, not a design-time commitment.\\\\n\\\\n## Design Principles\\\\n\\\\nCode quality is measured by malleability: how cheaply can changes adapt without breaking promises?\\\\nStigmergic coordination emerges from sharing data across streams.\\\\n\\\\n**Systems emerge from interpreters of pure data.** Streams are the\\\\ncomposition medium; each interpreter gives the same data a perspective\\\\nwithout collapsing interpretation into execution or owning the truth.\\\\n\\\\n- `dao.space` emerges from `dao.space.index` and `dao.space.query` over\\\\n  ordinary streams.\\\\n- ShiBi capability, metering, and budget emerge from different\\\\n  interpreters over the same tuples; no token object is stored.\\\\n- The four VMs interpret one Universal AST; many syntaxes feed that AST.\\\\n- The semantic AST in `dao.space` is queryable facts projected by the\\\\n  auto-index observer.\\\\n- Client and server are roles in one stigmergic behavior implemented by\\\\n  interpreters, not distinct kinds of nodes.\\\\n\\\\n**Derive, don't persist.** Before adding a tag, slot, or field to any\\\\ncanonical content-hashed structure (an AST grammar, a datom schema, a row\\\\nshape), check whether a correctly scoped Datalog query over\\\\n`dao.space.query/q` can already compute the fact. If it can, it belongs as a\\\\nquery or projection: new persisted structure migrates every downstream\\\\nconsumer and duplicates authority over a fact a query derives fresh. The\\\\nretired `:global` tag in\\\\n[`docs/design/yin.vm.code-as-tuples.md`](./yin.vm.code-as-tuples.md) is the\\\\ncase study, including the scoping bug that a naive query introduced.\\\\n\\\\nSee [`docs/agents/malleability.md`](../agents/malleability.md) for complete design guidance (cohesion, coupling, bounded complexity, evolution, testing strategy).\\\\nSee [`docs/agents/vocabulary.md`](../agents/vocabulary.md) for domain vocabulary reference (biology, economics, physics, philosophy).\\\\n\\\\n## Code Style\\\\n\\\\n- Prefer simple data over rich types.\\\\n- Prefer total functions over partial ones.\\\\n- Prefer declarative pipelines over imperative logic.\\\\n- Avoid cleverness.\\\\n- Name things after what they do to streams.\\\\n\\\\n## Development Workflow\\\\n\\\\n- Do not invent abstractions that hide streams.\\\\n- Do not suggest mainstream frameworks unless explicitly asked.\\\\n- Do not optimize prematurely.\\\\n- When uncertain, ask at the architectural level, not the implementation level.\\\\n- Explanations should align with Plan 9 / Datomic / Lisp lineage.\\\\n- Program store writes go through `engine/store-put`; any other store write\\\\n  the store-write audit (`test/yin/vm/store_write_audit_test.clj`)\\\\n  detects must be on its allowlist; its docstring states the residual it\\\\n  leaves to review.\\\\n\\\\n### Problem Decomposition\\\\n\\\\nIf a problem appears complex:\\\\n1. Decompose it into streams.\\\\n2. Identify invariants.\\\\n3. Restrict degrees of freedom.\\\\n4. Make causality explicit.\\\\n5. Let structure emerge from constraints.\\\\n\\\\n## Operational & Specialized Guides\\\\n\\\\n- **Advanced Concepts**: See [`docs/agents/advanced-concepts.md`](../agents/advanced-concepts.md) for parallel transport, capability tokens, and entanglement.\\\\n- **Build & Test**: See [`docs/agents/build-n-test.md`](../agents/build-n-test.md) for build, lint, and test commands and TDD guidelines.\\\\n- **Engineering Team Roster**: See [`docs/agents/team.md`](../agents/team.md) for engineering team roles and LLM model assignments.\\\\n- **Agent Delegation**: See [`docs/agents/roles/orchestrator.md`](../agents/roles/orchestrator.md) for collaboration protocols and delegating tasks or reviews through `agy`, `cmd`, `glm`, `deepseek`, and `codex`; the orchestrator's append-only work log is [`docs/orchestrator-log.md`](../orchestrator-log.md).\\\\n- **Website & Content**: See [`docs/agents/format.md`](../agents/format.md) for `.chp` and `.blog` EDN/Hiccup file specifications.\\\\n\\\",\\\"exit_code\\\":0,\\\"status\\\":\\\"completed\\\"}}\\n{\\\"type\\\":\\\"item.started\\\",\\\"item\\\":{\\\"id\\\":\\\"item_2\\\",\\\"type\\\":\\\"command_execution\\\",\\\"command\\\":\\\"/bin/zsh -lc 'nl -ba test/yin/vm/ucf/remote_test.cljc'\\\",\\\"aggregated_output\\\":\\\"\\\",\\\"exit_code\\\":null,\\\"status\\\":\\\"in_progress\\\"}}\\n{\\\"type\\\":\\\"item.completed\\\",\\\"item\\\":{\\\"id\\\":\\\"item_2\\\",\\\"type\\\":\\\"command_execution\\\",\\\"command\\\":\\\"/bin/zsh -lc 'nl -ba test/yin/vm/ucf/remote_test.cljc'\\\",\\\"aggregated_output\\\":\\\"     1\\\\t(ns yin.vm.ucf.remote-test\\\\n     2\\\\t  \\\\\\\"The slice 8 acceptance row\\\\n     3\\\\t   (`docs/design/dao.stream.remote.implementation-plan.md` slice 8;\\\\n     4\\\\t   `yin.vm.universal-continuation-format.md` S7.4.3, S7.5.3, S7.11.1\\\\n     5\\\\t   'Reflection acceptance'): a REAL machine parked through the engine\\\\n     6\\\\t   on a `:stream-next` wait migrates with a kept cursor and resumes\\\\n     7\\\\t   equivalently in a fresh engine state through a reflection; forced\\\\n     8\\\\t   eviction yields `gap` with the source's own recovery cursor; a\\\\n     9\\\\t   kept cursor that cannot survive the channel codec refuses the lift\\\\n    10\\\\t   before any cell is published; a source `serve!` refuses is\\\\n    11\\\\t   `:yin.k/unsatisfied`; an `attach!` that answers gone is\\\\n    12\\\\t   `:yin.k/unsatisfied` naming the stream at lower. Cursor cells are\\\\n    13\\\\t   minted and remapped across a whole frame set: two waiters on one\\\\n    14\\\\t   engine cell lift to one UCF cell and lower back shared, and\\\\n    15\\\\t   independent cells at one position stay independent (S7.5.3). The\\\\n    16\\\\t   remaining S7.4.3 variants -- `:put`, `:ffi`, `:ffi-request`,\\\\n    17\\\\t   `:link-request`, `:link-response`, `:install` -- round-trip\\\\n    18\\\\t   through stub `serve!`/`attach!` callbacks over the engine's own\\\\n    19\\\\t   wait-set shapes, since their proof is the shape of the bridge, not\\\\n    20\\\\t   the transport.\\\\\\\"\\\\n    21\\\\t  (:require [clojure.test :refer [deftest is testing]]\\\\n    22\\\\t            [dao.stream :as stream]\\\\n    23\\\\t            [dao.stream.apply :as apply2]\\\\n    24\\\\t            [dao.stream.remote :as remote]\\\\n    25\\\\t            [dao.stream.ringbuffer :as ringbuffer]\\\\n    26\\\\t            [yin.vm :as vm]\\\\n    27\\\\t            [yin.vm.linearize :as linearize]\\\\n    28\\\\t            [yin.vm.semantic :as semantic]\\\\n    29\\\\t            [yin.vm.ucf.remote :as ucf.remote]))\\\\n    30\\\\t\\\\n    31\\\\t\\\\n    32\\\\t;; =============================================================================\\\\n    33\\\\t;; The toy: two in-process ring buffers as the channel (as\\\\n    34\\\\t;; dao.stream.remote-test), with a served-table `serve!` on top\\\\n    35\\\\t;; =============================================================================\\\\n    36\\\\t\\\\n    37\\\\t(defn- ring\\\\n    38\\\\t  [capacity]\\\\n    39\\\\t  (:dao.stream/handle\\\\n    40\\\\t    (ringbuffer/create! {:dao.stream/type :dao.stream/ringbuffer\\\\n    41\\\\t                         :dao.stream.ringbuffer/capacity capacity})))\\\\n    42\\\\t\\\\n    43\\\\t\\\\n    44\\\\t(defn- toy\\\\n    45\\\\t  []\\\\n    46\\\\t  (let [ab (ring 64)\\\\n    47\\\\t        ba (ring 64)\\\\n    48\\\\t        cd {:dao.stream/type :dao.stream.test/channel\\\\n    49\\\\t            :dao.stream/identity \\\\\\\"ucf-remote-toy\\\\\\\"}]\\\\n    50\\\\t    {:channel cd, :ab ab, :ba ba,\\\\n    51\\\\t     :a-end {:reader ba, :writer ab},\\\\n    52\\\\t     :b-end {:reader ab, :writer ba}}))\\\\n    53\\\\t\\\\n    54\\\\t\\\\n    55\\\\t(defn- served-peer\\\\n    56\\\\t  [t]\\\\n    57\\\\t  {:table (atom {})\\\\n    58\\\\t   :b-reader (:reader (:b-end t))\\\\n    59\\\\t   :b-writer (:writer (:b-end t))\\\\n    60\\\\t   :mirror (atom (:dao.stream/cursor\\\\n    61\\\\t                   (stream/cursor (:reader (:b-end t)) :dao.stream/oldest)))})\\\\n    62\\\\t\\\\n    63\\\\t\\\\n    64\\\\t(defn- serve-mirror!\\\\n    65\\\\t  \\\\\\\"One mirror step over everything pending on the toy's request\\\\n    66\\\\t   buffer.\\\\\\\"\\\\n    67\\\\t  [peer]\\\\n    68\\\\t  (swap! (:mirror peer)\\\\n    69\\\\t         #(remote/mirror-step @(:table peer) (:b-reader peer) %\\\\n    70\\\\t                              (:b-writer peer))))\\\\n    71\\\\t\\\\n    72\\\\t\\\\n    73\\\\t(defn- server\\\\n    74\\\\t  \\\\\\\"The exporter's `serve!` (dao.stream.remote.md S2.3): assigns a\\\\n    75\\\\t   stable identity to `h`, entering it in the peer's table under\\\\n    76\\\\t   `chan`, if it is not already served.\\\\\\\"\\\\n    77\\\\t  [peer chan]\\\\n    78\\\\t  (fn [h]\\\\n    79\\\\t    (if-let [existing (some (fn [[id e]] (when (= h (:handle e)) id))\\\\n    80\\\\t                            @(:table peer))]\\\\n    81\\\\t      {:dao.stream/identity existing, :dao.stream/channel chan}\\\\n    82\\\\t      (let [id (str (gensym \\\\\\\"seg\\\\\\\"))]\\\\n    83\\\\t        (swap! (:table peer) assoc id {:handle h, :surface #{:reader}})\\\\n    84\\\\t        {:dao.stream/identity id, :dao.stream/channel chan}))))\\\\n    85\\\\t\\\\n    86\\\\t\\\\n    87\\\\t(defn- attacher\\\\n    88\\\\t  [t]\\\\n    89\\\\t  (remote/attacher\\\\n    90\\\\t    {:dao.stream.remote/channels {(:channel t) (:a-end t)}}))\\\\n    91\\\\t\\\\n    92\\\\t\\\\n    93\\\\t;; =============================================================================\\\\n    94\\\\t;; The emitter side: a real machine parked through the engine\\\\n    95\\\\t;; =============================================================================\\\\n    96\\\\t\\\\n    97\\\\t(def ^:private secret\\\\n    98\\\\t  \\\\\\\"The capability secret the test composition gives its machines.\\\\\\\"\\\\n    99\\\\t  \\\\\\\"yin.vm.ucf.remote-test/capability-secret\\\\\\\")\\\\n   100\\\\t\\\\n   101\\\\t\\\\n   102\\\\t(defn- make-ring-stream\\\\n   103\\\\t  \\\\\\\"The ring-buffer `:make-stream` this composition gives its\\\\n   104\\\\t   machines -- `yin.vm.test-utils`'s choice, at test scale.\\\\\\\"\\\\n   105\\\\t  [capacity]\\\\n   106\\\\t  (ringbuffer/create! {:dao.stream/type :dao.stream/ringbuffer\\\\n   107\\\\t                       :dao.stream.ringbuffer/capacity capacity}))\\\\n   108\\\\t\\\\n   109\\\\t\\\\n   110\\\\t(defn- new-machine\\\\n   111\\\\t  \\\\\\\"A fresh semantic machine over that composition.\\\\\\\"\\\\n   112\\\\t  []\\\\n   113\\\\t  (semantic/create-vm {:make-stream make-ring-stream\\\\n   114\\\\t                       :capability-secret secret}))\\\\n   115\\\\t\\\\n   116\\\\t\\\\n   117\\\\t(def ^:private load-ast\\\\n   118\\\\t  \\\\\\\"The trusted fresh path: the AST linearizer behind the code loader.\\\\\\\"\\\\n   119\\\\t  (vm/fresh-code-loader (linearize/ast-loader semantic/vm-load-program)\\\\n   120\\\\t                        vm/ast-contract))\\\\n   121\\\\t\\\\n   122\\\\t\\\\n   123\\\\t(defn- var-ref\\\\n   124\\\\t  [n]\\\\n   125\\\\t  {:type :variable, :name n})\\\\n   126\\\\t\\\\n   127\\\\t\\\\n   128\\\\t(defn- let1\\\\n   129\\\\t  \\\\\\\"`((fn [param] body) init)`.\\\\\\\"\\\\n   130\\\\t  [param init body]\\\\n   131\\\\t  {:type :application,\\\\n   132\\\\t   :operator {:type :lambda, :params [param], :body body},\\\\n   133\\\\t   :operands [init]})\\\\n   134\\\\t\\\\n   135\\\\t\\\\n   136\\\\t(defn- reader-datoms\\\\n   137\\\\t  \\\\\\\"Make a stream of `capacity`, mint a cursor on it, read one value.\\\\\\\"\\\\n   138\\\\t  [capacity]\\\\n   139\\\\t  (vm/ast->datoms\\\\n   140\\\\t    (let1 's {:type :stream/make, :buffer capacity}\\\\n   141\\\\t          {:type :stream/next,\\\\n   142\\\\t           :source {:type :stream/cursor, :source (var-ref 's)}})))\\\\n   143\\\\t\\\\n   144\\\\t\\\\n   145\\\\t(defn- parked-reader\\\\n   146\\\\t  \\\\\\\"A real machine parked through the engine on a `:stream-next` wait\\\\n   147\\\\t   over a fresh ring buffer: the code datoms, the parked VM, its\\\\n   148\\\\t   wait-set entry, and the stream handle the entry polls.\\\\\\\"\\\\n   149\\\\t  [capacity]\\\\n   150\\\\t  (let [datoms (reader-datoms capacity)\\\\n   151\\\\t        parked (vm/run (load-ast (new-machine) datoms))\\\\n   152\\\\t        entry (first (:wait-set parked))]\\\\n   153\\\\t    [datoms parked entry\\\\n   154\\\\t     (get (:resources parked) (:stream-id entry))]))\\\\n   155\\\\t\\\\n   156\\\\t\\\\n   157\\\\t(defn- registers-of\\\\n   158\\\\t  \\\\\\\"The register payload a parked entry carries.\\\\\\\"\\\\n   159\\\\t  [entry]\\\\n   160\\\\t  (select-keys entry [:segment :pc :env :stack :k]))\\\\n   161\\\\t\\\\n   162\\\\t\\\\n   163\\\\t(defn- quiesced-receiver\\\\n   164\\\\t  \\\\\\\"The fresh engine state a lower installs into: a real machine over\\\\n   165\\\\t   the same code image, quiesced, holding the lowered resource table\\\\n   166\\\\t   and the lowered wait-set entry -- nothing of the emitter's state\\\\n   167\\\\t   but the code image and the registers the entry carries.\\\\\\\"\\\\n   168\\\\t  [datoms lowered]\\\\n   169\\\\t  (assoc (load-ast (new-machine) datoms)\\\\n   170\\\\t         :control nil, :k nil,\\\\n   171\\\\t         :value :yin/blocked, :blocked? true, :halted? false,\\\\n   172\\\\t         :wait-set [(:entry lowered)],\\\\n   173\\\\t         :resources (:resources lowered)))\\\\n   174\\\\t\\\\n   175\\\\t\\\\n   176\\\\t(defn- cursor-entries\\\\n   177\\\\t  \\\\\\\"The cursor entries of a lowered resource table: maps keyed by the\\\\n   178\\\\t   UCF cell ids, each carrying its stream id and kept cursor.\\\\\\\"\\\\n   179\\\\t  [table]\\\\n   180\\\\t  (into {} (filter (fn [[_ v]] (and (map? v) (contains? v :stream-id))))\\\\n   181\\\\t        table))\\\\n   182\\\\t\\\\n   183\\\\t\\\\n   184\\\\t;; =============================================================================\\\\n   185\\\\t;; The acceptance row: a real parked machine migrates and resumes\\\\n   186\\\\t;; =============================================================================\\\\n   187\\\\t\\\\n   188\\\\t(deftest migrates-a-real-parked-machine-and-resumes\\\\n   189\\\\t  (let [t (toy)\\\\n   190\\\\t        peer (served-peer t)\\\\n   191\\\\t        serve! (server peer (:channel t))\\\\n   192\\\\t        attach! (attacher t)\\\\n   193\\\\t        [datoms parked entry src] (parked-reader 4)\\\\n   194\\\\t        cid (:id (:cursor-ref entry))\\\\n   195\\\\t        sid (:stream-id entry)\\\\n   196\\\\t        kept (get-in parked [:resources cid :cursor])\\\\n   197\\\\t        lifted (ucf.remote/lift-pending serve! (:resources parked) entry)\\\\n   198\\\\t        lowered (ucf.remote/lower-pending attach! (:yin.k/pending lifted)\\\\n   199\\\\t                                          (:yin.k/cells lifted)\\\\n   200\\\\t                                          (registers-of entry))\\\\n   201\\\\t        receiver (quiesced-receiver datoms lowered)]\\\\n   202\\\\t    (testing \\\\\\\"the machine parked through the engine\\\\\\\"\\\\n   203\\\\t      (is (vm/blocked? parked))\\\\n   204\\\\t      (is (= :next (:reason entry)))\\\\n   205\\\\t      (is (= :cursor-ref (get-in entry [:cursor-ref :type]))))\\\\n   206\\\\t    (testing \\\\\\\"the lift reads the engine's own wait-set entry\\\\\\\"\\\\n   207\\\\t      (is (= {:yin.k/reason :next, :yin.k/cell :yin.k/c-0}\\\\n   208\\\\t             (:yin.k/pending lifted))\\\\n   209\\\\t          \\\\\\\"the cursor CELL id, S7.5.3 -- not a bare position\\\\\\\")\\\\n   210\\\\t      (is (= kept (get-in lifted [:yin.k/cells :yin.k/c-0 :yin.k/position]))\\\\n   211\\\\t          \\\\\\\"the cell carries the engine's kept cursor\\\\\\\")\\\\n   212\\\\t      (is (= #{:dao.stream.remote/v1}\\\\n   213\\\\t             (get-in lifted [:yin.k/requires :yin.k/cursor-profiles]))))\\\\n   214\\\\t    (testing \\\\\\\"the lower builds a fresh engine state\\\\\\\"\\\\n   215\\\\t      (let [e (:entry lowered)\\\\n   216\\\\t            rs (:resources lowered)\\\\n   217\\\\t            cid' (get-in e [:cursor-ref :id])\\\\n   218\\\\t            sid' (:stream-id e)]\\\\n   219\\\\t        (is (= (registers-of entry) (registers-of e))\\\\n   220\\\\t            \\\\\\\"the register context rides the lower verbatim\\\\\\\")\\\\n   221\\\\t        (is (not= cid cid'))\\\\n   222\\\\t        (is (not= sid sid'))\\\\n   223\\\\t        (is (not (contains? rs cid)))\\\\n   224\\\\t        (is (not (contains? rs sid)))\\\\n   225\\\\t        (is (= {:stream-id sid', :cursor kept} (get rs cid'))\\\\n   226\\\\t            \\\\\\\"one fresh cursor entry, at the kept position\\\\\\\")\\\\n   227\\\\t        (is (not= src (get rs sid'))\\\\n   228\\\\t            \\\\\\\"the stream entry is a reflection, not the emitter's handle\\\\\\\")\\\\n   229\\\\t        (is (= sid' (get-in rs [cid' :stream-id])))))\\\\n   230\\\\t    (testing \\\\\\\"the emitter's own wait resumes equivalently\\\\\\\"\\\\n   231\\\\t      (stream/append! src \\\\\\\"hello\\\\\\\")\\\\n   232\\\\t      (is (= \\\\\\\"hello\\\\\\\" (vm/value (vm/run parked)))))\\\\n   233\\\\t    (testing \\\\\\\"the migrated wait resumes in the fresh engine state\\\\\\\"\\\\n   234\\\\t      (is (vm/blocked? (vm/run receiver))\\\\n   235\\\\t          \\\\\\\"the reflection answers blocked until the mirror serves\\\\\\\")\\\\n   236\\\\t      (serve-mirror! peer)\\\\n   237\\\\t      (let [done (vm/run receiver)]\\\\n   238\\\\t        (is (vm/halted? done))\\\\n   239\\\\t        (is (= \\\\\\\"hello\\\\\\\" (vm/value done))\\\\n   240\\\\t            \\\\\\\"the source's own value, through the kept cursor\\\\\\\")\\\\n   241\\\\t        (is (empty? (:wait-set done)))))))\\\\n   242\\\\t\\\\n   243\\\\t\\\\n   244\\\\t(deftest forced-eviction-yields-gap-with-the-sources-cursor\\\\n   245\\\\t  (let [t (toy)\\\\n   246\\\\t        peer (served-peer t)\\\\n   247\\\\t        serve! (server peer (:channel t))\\\\n   248\\\\t        attach! (attacher t)\\\\n   249\\\\t        [datoms parked entry src] (parked-reader 2)\\\\n   250\\\\t        cid (:id (:cursor-ref entry))\\\\n   251\\\\t        kept (get-in parked [:resources cid :cursor])\\\\n   252\\\\t        lifted (ucf.remote/lift-pending serve! (:resources parked) entry)\\\\n   253\\\\t        lowered (ucf.remote/lower-pending attach! (:yin.k/pending lifted)\\\\n   254\\\\t                                          (:yin.k/cells lifted)\\\\n   255\\\\t                                          (registers-of entry))\\\\n   256\\\\t        cid' (get-in (:entry lowered) [:cursor-ref :id])\\\\n   257\\\\t        receiver (quiesced-receiver datoms lowered)]\\\\n   258\\\\t    (stream/append! src \\\\\\\"hello\\\\\\\")\\\\n   259\\\\t    (doseq [v [\\\\\\\"v1\\\\\\\" \\\\\\\"v2\\\\\\\" \\\\\\\"v3\\\\\\\"]]\\\\n   260\\\\t      (stream/append! src v))\\\\n   261\\\\t    (is (vm/blocked? (vm/run receiver)))\\\\n   262\\\\t    (serve-mirror! peer)\\\\n   263\\\\t    (let [expected (stream/next src kept)\\\\n   264\\\\t          done (vm/run receiver)]\\\\n   265\\\\t      (testing \\\\\\\"the program reads the source's own gap, verbatim\\\\\\\"\\\\n   266\\\\t        (is (= :dao.stream/gap (vm/value done)))\\\\n   267\\\\t        (is (= (:dao.stream/cursor expected)\\\\n   268\\\\t               (get-in done [:resources cid' :cursor]))\\\\n   269\\\\t            \\\\\\\"with the source's own recovery cursor in the cell\\\\\\\"))\\\\n   270\\\\t      (testing \\\\\\\"no replay and no silent skip: the walk continues\\\\n   271\\\\t                from the recovery cursor\\\\\\\"\\\\n   272\\\\t        (let [r (get-in done [:resources (:stream-id (:entry lowered))])\\\\n   273\\\\t              recovery (get-in done [:resources cid' :cursor])]\\\\n   274\\\\t          (is (= :dao.stream/blocked\\\\n   275\\\\t                 (:dao.stream/outcome (stream/next r recovery))))\\\\n   276\\\\t          (serve-mirror! peer)\\\\n   277\\\\t          (let [ok (stream/next r recovery)]\\\\n   278\\\\t            (is (= :dao.stream/ok (:dao.stream/outcome ok)))\\\\n   279\\\\t            (is (= \\\\\\\"v2\\\\\\\" (:dao.stream/value ok)))))))))\\\\n   280\\\\t\\\\n   281\\\\t\\\\n   282\\\\t;; =============================================================================\\\\n   283\\\\t;; Unsatisfied: an unpublishable cursor, a source that cannot be\\\\n   284\\\\t;; served, a gone reflection\\\\n   285\\\\t;; =============================================================================\\\\n   286\\\\t\\\\n   287\\\\t(defn- host-cursor-stream\\\\n   288\\\\t  \\\\\\\"A handle whose cursors hold a host object -- the case\\\\n   289\\\\t   dao.stream.remote.md S2.3 says cannot be served.\\\\\\\"\\\\n   290\\\\t  []\\\\n   291\\\\t  (reify stream/IDaoStreamDescriptor\\\\n   292\\\\t    (descriptor\\\\n   293\\\\t      [_]\\\\n   294\\\\t      {:dao.stream/outcome :dao.stream/ok\\\\n   295\\\\t       :dao.stream/identity \\\\\\\"host-cursor\\\\\\\"\\\\n   296\\\\t       :dao.stream/descriptor\\\\n   297\\\\t       {:dao.stream/type :dao.stream.test/channel\\\\n   298\\\\t        :dao.stream/identity \\\\\\\"host-cursor\\\\\\\"}})\\\\n   299\\\\t\\\\n   300\\\\t\\\\n   301\\\\t    stream/IDaoStreamReader\\\\n   302\\\\t\\\\n   303\\\\t    (cursor\\\\n   304\\\\t      [_ _]\\\\n   305\\\\t      {:dao.stream/outcome :dao.stream/ok\\\\n   306\\\\t       :dao.stream/cursor {:position 0, :owner (fn [x] x)}})\\\\n   307\\\\t\\\\n   308\\\\t    (next\\\\n   309\\\\t      [_ _]\\\\n   310\\\\t      {:dao.stream/outcome :dao.stream/blocked})))\\\\n   311\\\\t\\\\n   312\\\\t\\\\n   313\\\\t(deftest a-cursor-that-cannot-round-trip-is-refused\\\\n   314\\\\t  (let [t (toy)\\\\n   315\\\\t        peer (served-peer t)\\\\n   316\\\\t        serve! (server peer (:channel t))\\\\n   317\\\\t        s (host-cursor-stream)\\\\n   318\\\\t        resources {:yin/host-stream s,\\\\n   319\\\\t                   :yin/host-cursor\\\\n   320\\\\t                   {:stream-id :yin/host-stream,\\\\n   321\\\\t                    :cursor {:position 0, :owner (fn [x] x)}}}\\\\n   322\\\\t        entry {:reason :next,\\\\n   323\\\\t               :cursor-ref {:type :cursor-ref, :id :yin/host-cursor},\\\\n   324\\\\t               :stream-id :yin/host-stream}\\\\n   325\\\\t        refusal (ucf.remote/lift-pending serve! resources entry)]\\\\n   326\\\\t    (is (= :yin.k/unsatisfied (:yin.k/status refusal))\\\\n   327\\\\t        \\\\\\\"the profile claim is checked before anything is published\\\\\\\")\\\\n   328\\\\t    (is (= \\\\\\\"host-cursor\\\\\\\" (:dao.stream/identity refusal))\\\\n   329\\\\t        \\\\\\\"naming the stream identity\\\\\\\")\\\\n   330\\\\t    (is (empty? @(:table peer))\\\\n   331\\\\t        \\\\\\\"refused before `serve!` even mints the descriptor\\\\\\\")))\\\\n   332\\\\t\\\\n   333\\\\t\\\\n   334\\\\t(deftest lift-refuses-unsatisfied-when-the-source-cannot-be-served\\\\n   335\\\\t  (let [s (ring 4)]\\\\n   336\\\\t    (stream/append! s \\\\\\\"x\\\\\\\")\\\\n   337\\\\t    (let [c0 (:dao.stream/cursor (stream/cursor s :dao.stream/oldest))\\\\n   338\\\\t          resources {:yin/s s, :yin/c {:stream-id :yin/s, :cursor c0}}\\\\n   339\\\\t          entry {:reason :next,\\\\n   340\\\\t                 :cursor-ref {:type :cursor-ref, :id :yin/c},\\\\n   341\\\\t                 :stream-id :yin/s}\\\\n   342\\\\t          refusal (ucf.remote/lift-pending (constantly nil) resources entry)]\\\\n   343\\\\t      (is (= :yin.k/unsatisfied (:yin.k/status refusal))\\\\n   344\\\\t          \\\\\\\"lift refuses before minting the value\\\\\\\")\\\\n   345\\\\t      (is (contains? refusal :dao.stream/identity)\\\\n   346\\\\t          \\\\\\\"naming the stream identity\\\\\\\"))))\\\\n   347\\\\t\\\\n   348\\\\t\\\\n   349\\\\t(deftest lower-refuses-unsatisfied-when-the-reflection-is-gone\\\\n   350\\\\t  (let [attach! (constantly {:dao.stream/outcome :dao.stream/transport-error\\\\n   351\\\\t                             :dao.stream.remote/reason\\\\n   352\\\\t                             :dao.stream.remote/not-found})\\\\n   353\\\\t        marker {:yin.k/tag :yin.k/stream,\\\\n   354\\\\t                :dao.stream/identity \\\\\\\"missing\\\\\\\",\\\\n   355\\\\t                :dao.stream/descriptor\\\\n   356\\\\t                {:dao.stream/type :dao.stream/remote,\\\\n   357\\\\t                 :dao.stream/identity \\\\\\\"missing\\\\\\\",\\\\n   358\\\\t                 :dao.stream/channel\\\\n   359\\\\t                 {:dao.stream/type :dao.stream.test/channel,\\\\n   360\\\\t                  :dao.stream/identity \\\\\\\"elsewhere\\\\\\\"}}}\\\\n   361\\\\t        pending {:yin.k/reason :next, :yin.k/cell :yin.k/c-0}\\\\n   362\\\\t        cells {:yin.k/c-0 {:yin.k/stream marker, :yin.k/position 0}}\\\\n   363\\\\t        lowered (ucf.remote/lower-pending attach! pending cells {})]\\\\n   364\\\\t    (is (= :yin.k/unsatisfied (:yin.k/status lowered)))\\\\n   365\\\\t    (is (= \\\\\\\"missing\\\\\\\" (:dao.stream/identity lowered))\\\\n   366\\\\t        \\\\\\\"naming the stream identity\\\\\\\")))\\\\n   367\\\\t\\\\n   368\\\\t\\\\n   369\\\\t;; =============================================================================\\\\n   370\\\\t;; Frame-level cells (S7.5.3): shared and independent\\\\n   371\\\\t;; =============================================================================\\\\n   372\\\\t\\\\n   373\\\\t(defn- stub-serve!\\\\n   374\\\\t  \\\\\\\"A `serve!` that assigns every handle to one identity per handle\\\\n   375\\\\t   under `chan`, with no wire underneath: these variants prove the\\\\n   376\\\\t   bridge's shape, the transport already proven above.\\\\\\\"\\\\n   377\\\\t  [chan]\\\\n   378\\\\t  (let [ids (atom {})]\\\\n   379\\\\t    (fn [h]\\\\n   380\\\\t      (let [id (or (get @ids h)\\\\n   381\\\\t                   (let [n (str (gensym \\\\\\\"seg\\\\\\\"))]\\\\n   382\\\\t                     (swap! ids assoc h n)\\\\n   383\\\\t                     n))]\\\\n   384\\\\t        {:dao.stream/identity id, :dao.stream/channel chan}))))\\\\n   385\\\\t\\\\n   386\\\\t\\\\n   387\\\\t(defn- stub-attach!\\\\n   388\\\\t  \\\\\\\"An `attach!` that answers ok at once with a reflection standing for\\\\n   389\\\\t   the descriptor's identity -- opaque here, since these variants\\\\n   390\\\\t   never poll it.\\\\\\\"\\\\n   391\\\\t  []\\\\n   392\\\\t  (fn [d]\\\\n   393\\\\t    {:dao.stream/outcome :dao.stream/ok,\\\\n   394\\\\t     :dao.stream/handle [:reflection-of (:dao.stream/identity d)]}))\\\\n   395\\\\t\\\\n   396\\\\t\\\\n   397\\\\t(def ^:private chan\\\\n   398\\\\t  {:dao.stream/type :dao.stream.test/channel, :dao.stream/identity \\\\\\\"c\\\\\\\"})\\\\n   399\\\\t\\\\n   400\\\\t\\\\n   401\\\\t(deftest shared-cursor-cells-lift-and-lower-shared\\\\n   402\\\\t  (let [serve! (stub-serve! chan)\\\\n   403\\\\t        attach! (stub-attach!)\\\\n   404\\\\t        [_datoms parked entry _src] (parked-reader 4)\\\\n   405\\\\t        cid (:id (:cursor-ref entry))\\\\n   406\\\\t        ;; a second waiter on the SAME engine cursor cell, as\\\\n   407\\\\t        ;; check-wait-set's shared-cursor co-waiters hold\\\\n   408\\\\t        second (assoc (registers-of entry)\\\\n   409\\\\t                      :reason :next,\\\\n   410\\\\t                      :stream-id (:stream-id entry),\\\\n   411\\\\t                      :cursor-ref {:type :cursor-ref, :id cid},\\\\n   412\\\\t                      :pc 42)\\\\n   413\\\\t        lifted (ucf.remote/lift-frame serve! (:resources parked)\\\\n   414\\\\t                                      [entry second])]\\\\n   415\\\\t    (testing \\\\\\\"two waiters on one engine cell lift to one UCF cell\\\\\\\"\\\\n   416\\\\t      (is (= 1 (count (:yin.k/cells lifted))))\\\\n   417\\\\t      (let [[p1 p2] (:yin.k/pending lifted)]\\\\n   418\\\\t        (is (= (:yin.k/cell p1) (:yin.k/cell p2))\\\\n   419\\\\t            \\\\\\\"both waiters name the one cell\\\\\\\")))\\\\n   420\\\\t    (let [ctxs [(registers-of entry) (registers-of second)]\\\\n   421\\\\t          lowered (ucf.remote/lower-frame attach! (:yin.k/pending lifted)\\\\n   422\\\\t                                          (:yin.k/cells lifted) ctxs)\\\\n   423\\\\t          [e1 e2] (:entries lowered)\\\\n   424\\\\t          rs (:resources lowered)]\\\\n   425\\\\t      (testing \\\\\\\"and lower back into one shared cursor entry\\\\\\\"\\\\n   426\\\\t        (is (= (get-in e1 [:cursor-ref :id])\\\\n   427\\\\t               (get-in e2 [:cursor-ref :id]))\\\\n   428\\\\t            \\\\\\\"one cell id stands for the one entry\\\\\\\")\\\\n   429\\\\t        (is (= 1 (count (cursor-entries rs)))))\\\\n   430\\\\t      (testing \\\\\\\"each entry keeps its own register context\\\\\\\"\\\\n   431\\\\t        (is (= (:pc entry) (:pc e1)))\\\\n   432\\\\t        (is (= 42 (:pc e2)))))))\\\\n   433\\\\t\\\\n   434\\\\t\\\\n   435\\\\t(deftest independent-cells-at-one-position-stay-independent\\\\n   436\\\\t  (let [serve! (stub-serve! chan)\\\\n   437\\\\t        attach! (stub-attach!)\\\\n   438\\\\t        s (ring 8)\\\\n   439\\\\t        _ (stream/append! s \\\\\\\"v\\\\\\\")\\\\n   440\\\\t        c0 (:dao.stream/cursor (stream/cursor s :dao.stream/oldest))\\\\n   441\\\\t        resources {:yin/s s,\\\\n   442\\\\t                   :yin/c1 {:stream-id :yin/s, :cursor c0},\\\\n   443\\\\t                   :yin/c2 {:stream-id :yin/s, :cursor c0}}\\\\n   444\\\\t        entry1 {:reason :next,\\\\n   445\\\\t                :cursor-ref {:type :cursor-ref, :id :yin/c1},\\\\n   446\\\\t                :stream-id :yin/s}\\\\n   447\\\\t        entry2 {:reason :next,\\\\n   448\\\\t                :cursor-ref {:type :cursor-ref, :id :yin/c2},\\\\n   449\\\\t                :stream-id :yin/s}\\\\n   450\\\\t        lifted (ucf.remote/lift-frame serve! resources\\\\n   451\\\\t                                      [entry1 entry2])]\\\\n   452\\\\t    (testing \\\\\\\"two engine cells at one position are two UCF cells\\\\\\\"\\\\n   453\\\\t      (is (= 2 (count (:yin.k/cells lifted)))\\\\n   454\\\\t          \\\\\\\"the aliasing a position-only encoding erases, kept\\\\\\\")\\\\n   455\\\\t      (let [[p1 p2] (:yin.k/pending lifted)]\\\\n   456\\\\t        (is (not= (:yin.k/cell p1) (:yin.k/cell p2)))\\\\n   457\\\\t        (is (= c0 (get-in lifted [:yin.k/cells (:yin.k/cell p1)\\\\n   458\\\\t                                  :yin.k/position])))\\\\n   459\\\\t        (is (= c0 (get-in lifted [:yin.k/cells (:yin.k/cell p2)\\\\n   460\\\\t                                  :yin.k/position])))))\\\\n   461\\\\t    (let [ctx {:segment 0, :pc 1, :env {}, :stack [], :k []}\\\\n   462\\\\t          lowered (ucf.remote/lower-frame attach! (:yin.k/pending lifted)\\\\n   463\\\\t                                          (:yin.k/cells lifted)\\\\n   464\\\\t                                          [ctx ctx])\\\\n   465\\\\t          [e1 e2] (:entries lowered)\\\\n   466\\\\t          rs (:resources lowered)]\\\\n   467\\\\t      (testing \\\\\\\"and lower into two independently advanceable entries\\\\\\\"\\\\n   468\\\\t        (is (not= (get-in e1 [:cursor-ref :id])\\\\n   469\\\\t                  (get-in e2 [:cursor-ref :id])))\\\\n   470\\\\t        (is (= 2 (count (cursor-entries rs))))\\\\n   471\\\\t        (is (= 1 (count (filter vector? (vals rs))))\\\\n   472\\\\t            \\\\\\\"one stream, so the two cells share one reflection\\\\\\\")))))\\\\n   473\\\\t\\\\n   474\\\\t\\\\n   475\\\\t(deftest a-refused-leaf-refuses-the-frame\\\\n   476\\\\t  (let [serve! (stub-serve! chan)\\\\n   477\\\\t        s (ring 4)\\\\n   478\\\\t        c0 (:dao.stream/cursor (stream/cursor s :dao.stream/oldest))\\\\n   479\\\\t        resources {:yin/s s, :yin/c {:stream-id :yin/s, :cursor c0}}\\\\n   480\\\\t        good {:reason :next,\\\\n   481\\\\t              :cursor-ref {:type :cursor-ref, :id :yin/c},\\\\n   482\\\\t              :stream-id :yin/s}]\\\\n   483\\\\t    (is (= :yin.k/undecodable\\\\n   484\\\\t           (:yin.k/status\\\\n   485\\\\t             (ucf.remote/lift-frame serve! resources\\\\n   486\\\\t                                    [good {:reason :bogus}])))\\\\n   487\\\\t        \\\\\\\"an unrecognized reason is total, S7.5.4\\\\\\\")\\\\n   488\\\\t    (is (= :yin.k/unsatisfied\\\\n   489\\\\t           (:yin.k/status\\\\n   490\\\\t             (ucf.remote/lift-frame (constantly nil) resources [good]))))))\\\\n   491\\\\t\\\\n   492\\\\t\\\\n   493\\\\t;; =============================================================================\\\\n   494\\\\t;; The remaining S7.4.3 variants round-trip, over the engine's shapes\\\\n   495\\\\t;; =============================================================================\\\\n   496\\\\t\\\\n   497\\\\t(deftest a-blocked-read-round-trips\\\\n   498\\\\t  (let [serve! (stub-serve! chan)\\\\n   499\\\\t        attach! (stub-attach!)\\\\n   500\\\\t        resources {:yin/s [:handle :s],\\\\n   501\\\\t                   :yin/c {:stream-id :yin/s, :cursor :kept-position}}\\\\n   502\\\\t        entry {:reason :next,\\\\n   503\\\\t               :cursor-ref {:type :cursor-ref, :id :yin/c},\\\\n   504\\\\t               :stream-id :yin/s}\\\\n   505\\\\t        lifted (ucf.remote/lift-pending serve! resources entry)]\\\\n   506\\\\t    (is (= {:yin.k/reason :next, :yin.k/cell :yin.k/c-0}\\\\n   507\\\\t           (:yin.k/pending lifted))\\\\n   508\\\\t        \\\\\\\"the cursor CELL id, S7.5.3 -- not a bare position\\\\\\\")\\\\n   509\\\\t    (is (= :kept-position\\\\n   510\\\\t           (get-in lifted [:yin.k/cells :yin.k/c-0 :yin.k/position])))\\\\n   511\\\\t    (is (= #{:dao.stream.remote/v1}\\\\n   512\\\\t           (get-in lifted [:yin.k/requires :yin.k/cursor-profiles])))\\\\n   513\\\\t    (let [ctx {:segment 0, :pc 7, :env {}, :stack [], :k []}\\\\n   514\\\\t          lowered (ucf.remote/lower-pending attach! (:yin.k/pending lifted)\\\\n   515\\\\t                                            (:yin.k/cells lifted) ctx)\\\\n   516\\\\t          e (:entry lowered)]\\\\n   517\\\\t      (is (= :next (:reason e)))\\\\n   518\\\\t      (is (= 7 (:pc e)) \\\\\\\"the registers ride the lower\\\\\\\")\\\\n   519\\\\t      (is (= :yin.k/c-0 (get-in e [:cursor-ref :id])))\\\\n   520\\\\t      (is (contains? (:resources lowered) (:stream-id e)))\\\\n   521\\\\t      (is (= :kept-position\\\\n   522\\\\t             (get-in lowered [:resources (get-in e [:cursor-ref :id])\\\\n   523\\\\t                              :cursor]))))))\\\\n   524\\\\t\\\\n   525\\\\t\\\\n   526\\\\t(deftest put-round-trips\\\\n   527\\\\t  (let [serve! (stub-serve! chan)\\\\n   528\\\\t        attach! (stub-attach!)\\\\n   529\\\\t        resources {:yin/w [:handle :w]}\\\\n   530\\\\t        entry {:reason :put, :stream-id :yin/w, :datom \\\\\\\"hello\\\\\\\"}\\\\n   531\\\\t        lifted (ucf.remote/lift-pending serve! resources entry)]\\\\n   532\\\\t    (is (= :put (get-in lifted [:yin.k/pending :yin.k/reason])))\\\\n   533\\\\t    (is (= \\\\\\\"hello\\\\\\\" (get-in lifted [:yin.k/pending :yin.k/value]))\\\\n   534\\\\t        \\\\\\\"the retained :datom -- a retry appends THIS\\\\\\\")\\\\n   535\\\\t    (is (empty? (:yin.k/cells lifted))\\\\n   536\\\\t        \\\\\\\"a put wait names a stream, never a cursor cell\\\\\\\")\\\\n   537\\\\t    (is (empty? (:yin.k/requires lifted)))\\\\n   538\\\\t    (let [ctx {:segment 0, :pc 3, :env {}, :stack [], :k []}\\\\n   539\\\\t          lowered (ucf.remote/lower-pending attach! (:yin.k/pending lifted)\\\\n   540\\\\t                                            (:yin.k/cells lifted) ctx)\\\\n   541\\\\t          e (:entry lowered)]\\\\n   542\\\\t      (is (= :put (:reason e)))\\\\n   543\\\\t      (is (= \\\\\\\"hello\\\\\\\" (:datom e)))\\\\n   544\\\\t      (is (contains? (:resources lowered) (:stream-id e))\\\\n   545\\\\t          \\\\\\\"the target is a fresh reflection resource\\\\\\\"))))\\\\n   546\\\\t\\\\n   547\\\\t\\\\n   548\\\\t(deftest ffi-sent-round-trips\\\\n   549\\\\t  (let [serve! (stub-serve! chan)\\\\n   550\\\\t        attach! (stub-attach!)\\\\n   551\\\\t        resources {:yin/call-out [:handle :call-out],\\\\n   552\\\\t                   :yin/call-out-cursor\\\\n   553\\\\t                   {:stream-id :yin/call-out, :cursor 5}}\\\\n   554\\\\t        entry {:reason :next, :call-id :call-7, :op :op/add,\\\\n   555\\\\t               :cursor-ref {:type :cursor-ref, :id :yin/call-out-cursor},\\\\n   556\\\\t               :stream-id :yin/call-out}\\\\n   557\\\\t        lifted (ucf.remote/lift-pending serve! resources entry)\\\\n   558\\\\t        pending (:yin.k/pending lifted)]\\\\n   559\\\\t    (is (= :ffi (:yin.k/reason pending)))\\\\n   560\\\\t    (is (= :call-7 (:yin.k/call-id pending)))\\\\n   561\\\\t    (is (= :op/add (:yin.k/op pending)))\\\\n   562\\\\t    (is (= :yin.k/c-0 (:yin.k/cell pending)))\\\\n   563\\\\t    (is (= 5 (get-in lifted [:yin.k/cells :yin.k/c-0 :yin.k/position]))\\\\n   564\\\\t        \\\\\\\"the response cell at its KEPT position\\\\\\\")\\\\n   565\\\\t    (let [ctx {:segment 0, :pc 9, :env {}, :stack [], :k []}\\\\n   566\\\\t          lowered (ucf.remote/lower-pending attach! pending\\\\n   567\\\\t                                            (:yin.k/cells lifted) ctx)\\\\n   568\\\\t          e (:entry lowered)]\\\\n   569\\\\t      (is (= :next (:reason e)) \\\\\\\"the response wait is a :next waiter\\\\\\\")\\\\n   570\\\\t      (is (= :call-7 (:call-id e)))\\\\n   571\\\\t      (is (= :op/add (:op e)))\\\\n   572\\\\t      (is (= :yin.k/c-0 (get-in e [:cursor-ref :id])))\\\\n   573\\\\t      (is (= 5 (get-in lowered [:resources (:yin.k/cell pending)\\\\n   574\\\\t                                :cursor]))))))\\\\n   575\\\\t\\\\n   576\\\\t\\\\n   577\\\\t(deftest ffi-retained-round-trips\\\\n   578\\\\t  (let [serve! (stub-serve! chan)\\\\n   579\\\\t        attach! (stub-attach!)\\\\n   580\\\\t        envelope (apply2/request :call-7 :op/add [1 2])\\\\n   581\\\\t        resources {:yin/call-in [:handle :call-in]}\\\\n   582\\\\t        entry {:reason :put, :request-sent true, :call-id :call-7,\\\\n   583\\\\t               :op :op/add, :stream-id :yin/call-in, :datom envelope}\\\\n   584\\\\t        lifted (ucf.remote/lift-pending serve! resources entry)\\\\n   585\\\\t        pending (:yin.k/pending lifted)]\\\\n   586\\\\t    (is (= :ffi-request (:yin.k/reason pending)))\\\\n   587\\\\t    (is (= :call-7 (:yin.k/call-id pending)))\\\\n   588\\\\t    (is (= :op/add (:yin.k/request-op pending)))\\\\n   589\\\\t    (is (= [1 2] (:yin.k/request-args pending)))\\\\n   590\\\\t    (is (empty? (:yin.k/cells lifted))\\\\n   591\\\\t        \\\\\\\"a retained request has no response cell yet\\\\\\\")\\\\n   592\\\\t    (let [ctx {:segment 0, :pc 5, :env {}, :stack [], :k []}\\\\n   593\\\\t          lowered (ucf.remote/lower-pending attach! pending\\\\n   594\\\\t                                            (:yin.k/cells lifted) ctx)\\\\n   595\\\\t          e (:entry lowered)]\\\\n   596\\\\t      (is (= :put (:reason e)))\\\\n   597\\\\t      (is (true? (:request-sent e)))\\\\n   598\\\\t      (is (= :call-7 (:call-id e)))\\\\n   599\\\\t      (is (= envelope (:datom e))\\\\n   600\\\\t          \\\\\\\"the envelope rebuilt verbatim under its call id\\\\\\\")\\\\n   601\\\\t      (is (contains? (:resources lowered) (:stream-id e))))))\\\\n   602\\\\t\\\\n   603\\\\t\\\\n   604\\\\t(deftest link-request-round-trips\\\\n   605\\\\t  (let [serve! (stub-serve! chan)\\\\n   606\\\\t        attach! (stub-attach!)\\\\n   607\\\\t        envelope {:yin.link/id [:t0 7], :yin.link/name 'foo,\\\\n   608\\\\t                  :yin.link/format :yin.debruijn.code,\\\\n   609\\\\t                  :yin.link/contract \\\\\\\"b2\\\\\\\"}\\\\n   610\\\\t        resources {:yin/link-req [:handle :req],\\\\n   611\\\\t                   :yin/link-resp [:handle :resp]}\\\\n   612\\\\t        entry {:reason :link-request, :link-id [:t0 7], :name 'foo,\\\\n   613\\\\t               :envelope envelope,\\\\n   614\\\\t               :request :yin/link-req, :response :yin/link-resp,\\\\n   615\\\\t               :cursor :dao.stream/newest}\\\\n   616\\\\t        lifted (ucf.remote/lift-pending serve! resources entry)\\\\n   617\\\\t        pending (:yin.k/pending lifted)]\\\\n   618\\\\t    (is (= :link-request (:yin.k/reason pending)))\\\\n   619\\\\t    (is (= [:t0 7] (:yin.k/link-id pending)))\\\\n   620\\\\t    (is (= 'foo (:yin.k/name pending)))\\\\n   621\\\\t    (is (= envelope (:yin.k/envelope pending)))\\\\n   622\\\\t    (is (= :dao.stream/newest\\\\n   623\\\\t           (get-in lifted [:yin.k/cells :yin.k/c-0 :yin.k/position]))\\\\n   624\\\\t        \\\\\\\"minted newest before the request was appended\\\\\\\")\\\\n   625\\\\t    (let [ctx {:segment 0, :pc 2, :env {}, :stack [], :k []}\\\\n   626\\\\t          lowered (ucf.remote/lower-pending attach! pending\\\\n   627\\\\t                                            (:yin.k/cells lifted) ctx)\\\\n   628\\\\t          e (:entry lowered)\\\\n   629\\\\t          rs (:resources lowered)]\\\\n   630\\\\t      (is (= :link-request (:reason e)))\\\\n   631\\\\t      (is (= envelope (:envelope e)))\\\\n   632\\\\t      (is (= :dao.stream/newest (:cursor e)))\\\\n   633\\\\t      (is (contains? rs (:request e)))\\\\n   634\\\\t      (is (= (:response e) (get-in rs [(:yin.k/cell pending) :stream-id]))\\\\n   635\\\\t          \\\\\\\"the response cell lowers onto the response reflection\\\\\\\"))))\\\\n   636\\\\t\\\\n   637\\\\t\\\\n   638\\\\t(deftest link-response-round-trips\\\\n   639\\\\t  (let [serve! (stub-serve! chan)\\\\n   640\\\\t        attach! (stub-attach!)\\\\n   641\\\\t        resources {:yin/link-req [:handle :req],\\\\n   642\\\\t                   :yin/link-resp [:handle :resp]}\\\\n   643\\\\t        entry {:reason :link-response, :link-id [:t0 7], :name 'foo,\\\\n   644\\\\t               :request :yin/link-req, :response :yin/link-resp,\\\\n   645\\\\t               :cursor 3}\\\\n   646\\\\t        lifted (ucf.remote/lift-pending serve! resources entry)\\\\n   647\\\\t        pending (:yin.k/pending lifted)]\\\\n   648\\\\t    (is (= :link-response (:yin.k/reason pending)))\\\\n   649\\\\t    (is (= [:t0 7] (:yin.k/link-id pending)))\\\\n   650\\\\t    (is (= 'foo (:yin.k/name pending)))\\\\n   651\\\\t    (is (= 3 (get-in lifted [:yin.k/cells :yin.k/c-0 :yin.k/position])))\\\\n   652\\\\t    (let [ctx {:segment 0, :pc 2, :env {}, :stack [], :k []}\\\\n   653\\\\t          lowered (ucf.remote/lower-pending attach! pending\\\\n   654\\\\t                                            (:yin.k/cells lifted) ctx)\\\\n   655\\\\t          e (:entry lowered)]\\\\n   656\\\\t      (is (= :link-response (:reason e)))\\\\n   657\\\\t      (is (= 3 (:cursor e)))\\\\n   658\\\\t      (is (contains? e :request) \\\\\\\"the pair fields the poll keeps\\\\\\\")\\\\n   659\\\\t      (is (contains? e :response))\\\\n   660\\\\t      (is (not (contains? e :envelope))\\\\n   661\\\\t          \\\\\\\"an appended request carries its envelope no more\\\\\\\"))))\\\\n   662\\\\t\\\\n   663\\\\t\\\\n   664\\\\t(deftest install-passes-through-unchanged\\\\n   665\\\\t  (let [entry {:reason :install, :name 'foo}\\\\n   666\\\\t        lifted (ucf.remote/lift-pending (constantly nil) {} entry)]\\\\n   667\\\\t    (is (= {:yin.k/reason :install, :yin.k/name 'foo}\\\\n   668\\\\t           (:yin.k/pending lifted)))\\\\n   669\\\\t    (is (empty? (:yin.k/cells lifted)))\\\\n   670\\\\t    (let [lowered (ucf.remote/lower-pending\\\\n   671\\\\t                    (constantly nil) (:yin.k/pending lifted) {}\\\\n   672\\\\t                    {:segment 0, :pc 3})]\\\\n   673\\\\t      (is (= {:reason :install, :name 'foo, :segment 0, :pc 3}\\\\n   674\\\\t             (:entry lowered))))))\\\\n   675\\\\t\\\\n   676\\\\t\\\\n   677\\\\t(deftest an-unrecognized-reason-is-undecodable\\\\n   678\\\\t  (is (= :yin.k/undecodable\\\\n   679\\\\t         (:yin.k/status (ucf.remote/lift-pending\\\\n   680\\\\t                          (constantly nil) {} {:reason :bogus}))))\\\\n   681\\\\t  (is (= :yin.k/undecodable\\\\n   682\\\\t         (:yin.k/status (ucf.remote/lower-pending\\\\n   683\\\\t                          (constantly nil) {:yin.k/reason :bogus} {}\\\\n   684\\\\t                          {})))))\\\\n\\\",\\\"exit_code\\\":0,\\\"status\\\":\\\"completed\\\"}}\\n{\\\"type\\\":\\\"item.started\\\",\\\"item\\\":{\\\"id\\\":\\\"item_3\\\",\\\"type\\\":\\\"command_execution\\\",\\\"command\\\":\\\"/bin/zsh -lc 'nl -ba src/cljc/yin/vm/ucf/remote.cljc'\\\",\\\"aggregated_output\\\":\\\"\\\",\\\"exit_code\\\":null,\\\"status\\\":\\\"in_progress\\\"}}\\n{\\\"type\\\":\\\"item.completed\\\",\\\"item\\\":{\\\"id\\\":\\\"item_3\\\",\\\"type\\\":\\\"command_execution\\\",\\\"command\\\":\\\"/bin/zsh -lc 'nl -ba src/cljc/yin/vm/ucf/remote.cljc'\\\",\\\"aggregated_output\\\":\\\"     1\\\\t(ns yin.vm.ucf.remote\\\\n     2\\\\t  \\\\\\\"The UCF facade through `dao.stream.remote` descriptors: lifts a\\\\n     3\\\\t   parked semantic machine's pending wait\\\\n     4\\\\t   (`docs/design/yin.vm.universal-continuation-format.md` S7.4.3) into\\\\n     5\\\\t   UCF data whose cells and stream markers name `dao.stream.remote`\\\\n     6\\\\t   descriptors under the `:dao.stream.remote/v1` cursor profile\\\\n     7\\\\t   (S7.5.3), and lowers that data back into a resumable local wait\\\\n     8\\\\t   through a reflection (`docs/design/dao.stream.remote.md` S2.2,\\\\n     9\\\\t   S2.4).\\\\n    10\\\\t\\\\n    11\\\\t   The local side is the engine's own parked machinery, not an\\\\n    12\\\\t   invented shape. A pending entry is what `yin.vm` parks: the\\\\n    13\\\\t   machine registers beside `:stream-id` and `:cursor-ref`\\\\n    14\\\\t   (`yin.vm.semantic` S3.5's park entries, `response-wait-entry`;\\\\n    15\\\\t   `yin.vm.engine`'s wait-set sweep), every handle and cursor\\\\n    16\\\\t   resolved out of the machine's private `:resources` table -- the\\\\n    17\\\\t   lift reads the table, and no entry ever carries a live handle.\\\\n    18\\\\t   The lower mirrors it: fresh resource entries, one per stream\\\\n    19\\\\t   reflection and one per cursor cell (two waiters sharing one cell\\\\n    20\\\\t   share the one entry, S7.5.3), and wait-set entries that merge the\\\\n    21\\\\t   caller's register context verbatim, so a lowered wait parks under\\\\n    22\\\\t   the engine's own sweep exactly as an unmigrated one does.\\\\n    23\\\\t\\\\n    24\\\\t   `lift-pending` and `lower-pending` are plain-data functions,\\\\n    25\\\\t   parameterized by two composition callbacks rather than coupled to\\\\n    26\\\\t   `yin.vm` or `dao.stream.remote` internals:\\\\n    27\\\\t\\\\n    28\\\\t     serve!  : handle -> {:dao.stream/identity id\\\\n    29\\\\t                          :dao.stream/channel chan} | nil\\\\n    30\\\\t               the exporter's own table entry\\\\n    31\\\\t               (`dao.stream.remote.md` S2.3): nil when the handle\\\\n    32\\\\t               cannot be served -- no table to enter it in, no\\\\n    33\\\\t               channel to the resumer -- which refuses the lift as\\\\n    34\\\\t               `:yin.k/unsatisfied` before minting the value\\\\n    35\\\\t               (S7.4.3).\\\\n    36\\\\t\\\\n    37\\\\t     attach! : remote-descriptor -> {:dao.stream/outcome\\\\n    38\\\\t                                     :dao.stream/ok\\\\n    39\\\\t                                     :dao.stream/handle reflection}\\\\n    40\\\\t               | outcome-map\\\\n    41\\\\t               the receiver's own `:dao.stream/attach` dispatch for\\\\n    42\\\\t               `:dao.stream/remote` (`dao.stream.remote.md` S2.4): an\\\\n    43\\\\t               outcome other than `ok` -- including a reflection\\\\n    44\\\\t               already marked gone -- refuses the lower as\\\\n    45\\\\t               `:yin.k/unsatisfied` naming the stream identity.\\\\n    46\\\\t\\\\n    47\\\\t   The `:dao.stream.remote/v1` claim is checked, not declared: a cell\\\\n    48\\\\t   is published only after its kept cursor survives a round trip\\\\n    49\\\\t   through the channel codec -- encoded, decoded back, equal -- which\\\\n    50\\\\t   is what plain data in the channel's portable domain means\\\\n    51\\\\t   (S7.4.3; `dao.stream.remote.md` S2.3's plain-data basis).\\\\n    52\\\\t   `cursor-codec` is the default codec; a composition whose channel\\\\n    53\\\\t   speaks another passes its own `{:encode f :decode f}` to\\\\n    54\\\\t   `lift-pending` or `lift-frame`. A cursor that does not round trip\\\\n    55\\\\t   -- a host object inside is the case S2.3 names -- refuses the lift\\\\n    56\\\\t   as `:yin.k/unsatisfied` before any value is minted.\\\\n    57\\\\t\\\\n    58\\\\t   Every pending variant of S7.4.3 lifts and lowers: `:next`, `:put`,\\\\n    59\\\\t   `:ffi`, `:ffi-request`, and the linker's `:link-request`,\\\\n    60\\\\t   `:link-response` and `:install` (`yin.vm.linker.md` S7.2-7.3).\\\\n    61\\\\t   `:install` names no stream and passes through unchanged.\\\\n    62\\\\t\\\\n    63\\\\t   Scope: `lift-frame` and `lower-frame` are the frame-level entry\\\\n    64\\\\t   points -- cells are minted and remapped across the WHOLE entry\\\\n    65\\\\t   set, so two waiters on one engine cursor cell lift to one UCF\\\\n    66\\\\t   cell and lower back into one shared cursor entry, and independent\\\\n    67\\\\t   cells stay independent (S7.5.3, and the sharing rule of the S7.11\\\\n    68\\\\t   pending-state blocker). `lift-pending` and `lower-pending` lift or\\\\n    69\\\\t   lower one entry into a self-contained table.\\\\\\\"\\\\n    70\\\\t  (:require [dao.stream :as stream]\\\\n    71\\\\t            [dao.stream.apply :as apply2]\\\\n    72\\\\t            [dao.stream.cbor :as cbor]))\\\\n    73\\\\t\\\\n    74\\\\t\\\\n    75\\\\t(def cursor-profiles\\\\n    76\\\\t  \\\\\\\"The one portable cursor profile S7.4.3 names in :yin.k/requires: a\\\\n    77\\\\t   cursor is plain data in the channel's portable domain and the\\\\n    78\\\\t   source honors it after serialization, cursor identity, position and\\\\n    79\\\\t   `gap` outcomes included.\\\\\\\"\\\\n    80\\\\t  #{:dao.stream.remote/v1})\\\\n    81\\\\t\\\\n    82\\\\t\\\\n    83\\\\t(def cursor-codec\\\\n    84\\\\t  \\\\\\\"The channel codec a lift round-trips kept cursors through when the\\\\n    85\\\\t   composition supplies none: the DaoStream v2 wire codec, whose\\\\n    86\\\\t   portable domain is the domain the profile claim names.\\\\\\\"\\\\n    87\\\\t  {:encode cbor/encode, :decode cbor/decode})\\\\n    88\\\\t\\\\n    89\\\\t\\\\n    90\\\\t(def ^:private requires\\\\n    91\\\\t  {:yin.k/cursor-profiles cursor-profiles})\\\\n    92\\\\t\\\\n    93\\\\t\\\\n    94\\\\t;; =============================================================================\\\\n    95\\\\t;; Markers (S7.5.1), through a remote descriptor\\\\n    96\\\\t;; =============================================================================\\\\n    97\\\\t\\\\n    98\\\\t(defn- local-identity\\\\n    99\\\\t  \\\\\\\"The identity `h` itself declares, when its descriptor answers ok;\\\\n   100\\\\t   nil otherwise -- the best name a refusal can give when `serve!` has\\\\n   101\\\\t   not minted one.\\\\\\\"\\\\n   102\\\\t  [h]\\\\n   103\\\\t  (let [d (when (stream/descriptor? h) (stream/descriptor h))]\\\\n   104\\\\t    (when (= :dao.stream/ok (:dao.stream/outcome d))\\\\n   105\\\\t      (:dao.stream/identity d))))\\\\n   106\\\\t\\\\n   107\\\\t\\\\n   108\\\\t(defn- unsatisfied\\\\n   109\\\\t  ([] (unsatisfied nil))\\\\n   110\\\\t  ([identity]\\\\n   111\\\\t   (cond-> {:yin.k/status :yin.k/unsatisfied}\\\\n   112\\\\t     (some? identity) (assoc :dao.stream/identity identity))))\\\\n   113\\\\t\\\\n   114\\\\t\\\\n   115\\\\t(defn- portable-cursor\\\\n   116\\\\t  \\\\\\\"The kept cursor when it survives a round trip through the channel\\\\n   117\\\\t   codec -- encoded, decoded back, and equal -- which is what the\\\\n   118\\\\t   `:dao.stream.remote/v1` claim means: plain data in the channel's\\\\n   119\\\\t   portable domain, honored after serialization. nil when it does\\\\n   120\\\\t   not, so no cell is ever published over an unpublishable cursor.\\\\\\\"\\\\n   121\\\\t  [codec cursor]\\\\n   122\\\\t  (try (let [w (:encode codec)\\\\n   123\\\\t             b (w cursor)\\\\n   124\\\\t             r ((:decode codec) b)]\\\\n   125\\\\t         (when (= cursor r) cursor))\\\\n   126\\\\t       (catch #?(:cljd Object :clj Throwable :cljs :default) _ nil)))\\\\n   127\\\\t\\\\n   128\\\\t\\\\n   129\\\\t(defn lift-marker\\\\n   130\\\\t  \\\\\\\"The UCF stream marker (S7.5.1) for local handle `h`, its descriptor\\\\n   131\\\\t   the remote descriptor `serve!` mints by entering `h` in the\\\\n   132\\\\t   exporter's table (`dao.stream.remote.md` S2.2). nil when `serve!`\\\\n   133\\\\t   refuses -- the source cannot be entered, or cannot honor the\\\\n   134\\\\t   profile -- so a caller mints `:yin.k/unsatisfied` before any value\\\\n   135\\\\t   is produced (S7.4.3).\\\\\\\"\\\\n   136\\\\t  [serve! h]\\\\n   137\\\\t  (when-let [served (serve! h)]\\\\n   138\\\\t    (let [id (:dao.stream/identity served)]\\\\n   139\\\\t      {:yin.k/tag :yin.k/stream,\\\\n   140\\\\t       :dao.stream/identity id,\\\\n   141\\\\t       :dao.stream/descriptor\\\\n   142\\\\t       {:dao.stream/type :dao.stream/remote,\\\\n   143\\\\t        :dao.stream/identity id,\\\\n   144\\\\t        :dao.stream/channel (:dao.stream/channel served)}})))\\\\n   145\\\\t\\\\n   146\\\\t\\\\n   147\\\\t(defn lower-marker\\\\n   148\\\\t  \\\\\\\"The local handle `attach!` gives for UCF stream marker `m` -- a\\\\n   149\\\\t   reflection on the original logical stream -- or nil when the attach\\\\n   150\\\\t   does not answer ok: a reflection marked gone, or any other refusal,\\\\n   151\\\\t   is unsatisfied at the caller.\\\\\\\"\\\\n   152\\\\t  [attach! m]\\\\n   153\\\\t  (let [result (attach! (:dao.stream/descriptor m))]\\\\n   154\\\\t    (when (= :dao.stream/ok (:dao.stream/outcome result))\\\\n   155\\\\t      (:dao.stream/handle result))))\\\\n   156\\\\t\\\\n   157\\\\t\\\\n   158\\\\t;; =============================================================================\\\\n   159\\\\t;; The pending wait (S7.4.3)\\\\n   160\\\\t;; =============================================================================\\\\n   161\\\\t;;\\\\n   162\\\\t;; Local pending-entry shapes this namespace lifts, and lowers back to\\\\n   163\\\\t;; -- the engine's own wait-set shapes, plain data resolved through\\\\n   164\\\\t;; the machine's `:resources` table:\\\\n   165\\\\t;;\\\\n   166\\\\t;;   {:reason :next          :cursor-ref {:type :cursor-ref, :id cid}\\\\n   167\\\\t;;                           :stream-id sid}          ; blocked read\\\\n   168\\\\t;;   {:reason :next          :call-id id :op op        ; a sent call's\\\\n   169\\\\t;;                           :cursor-ref {:type :cursor-ref, :id cid}\\\\n   170\\\\t;;                           :stream-id sid}          ; response wait\\\\n   171\\\\t;;   {:reason :put           :stream-id sid            ; blocked write,\\\\n   172\\\\t;;                           :datom v}                 ; :datom the retry\\\\n   173\\\\t;;   {:reason :put           :request-sent true        ; a retained FFI\\\\n   174\\\\t;;                           :call-id id :op op        ; request\\\\n   175\\\\t;;                           :stream-id sid :datom env}\\\\n   176\\\\t;;   {:reason :link-request  :link-id id :name m :envelope e\\\\n   177\\\\t;;                           :request rid :response rid' :cursor kept}\\\\n   178\\\\t;;   {:reason :link-response :link-id id :name m\\\\n   179\\\\t;;                           :request rid :response rid' :cursor kept}\\\\n   180\\\\t;;   {:reason :install       :name m}\\\\n   181\\\\t;;\\\\n   182\\\\t;; `cid` names a `:resources` cursor entry `{:stream-id sid :cursor\\\\n   183\\\\t;; kept}` (`vm/cursor-entry`); `sid` and `rid` name stream handles in\\\\n   184\\\\t;; the same table; `env` is the retained `dao.stream.apply` envelope.\\\\n   185\\\\t;; The registers every parked entry also carries -- :segment :pc :env\\\\n   186\\\\t;; :stack :k -- are the machine's own context: the lift ignores them\\\\n   187\\\\t;; (they travel in the frame's continuation slice, not the pending\\\\n   188\\\\t;; wait), and the lower stamps the caller's context back onto the\\\\n   189\\\\t;; entry it builds.\\\\n   190\\\\t\\\\n   191\\\\t\\\\n   192\\\\t;; =============================================================================\\\\n   193\\\\t;; Cell minting and remapping (S7.5.3), across the whole frame set\\\\n   194\\\\t;; =============================================================================\\\\n   195\\\\t\\\\n   196\\\\t(defn- mint-cell\\\\n   197\\\\t  \\\\\\\"One mint per distinct cursor cell across the WHOLE frame set:\\\\n   198\\\\t   `found` accumulates the remapping {cell key -> UCF cell id} beside\\\\n   199\\\\t   the cells themselves as entries lift, so two waiters on one\\\\n   200\\\\t   engine cursor cell lift to one UCF cell, and independent cells\\\\n   201\\\\t   stay independent, whatever their positions (S7.5.3). `k` is the\\\\n   202\\\\t   cell's identity -- the engine cursor resource id a `:next` waiter\\\\n   203\\\\t   names, or the response stream and kept cursor a link wait names.\\\\n   204\\\\t   The cell carries the marker `serve!` mints for the cell's stream\\\\n   205\\\\t   and its kept cursor, published only after the cursor survives the\\\\n   206\\\\t   codec round trip; nil -- refuse -- when it does not, or when\\\\n   207\\\\t   `serve!` refuses the stream.\\\\\\\"\\\\n   208\\\\t  [serve! found]\\\\n   209\\\\t  (fn [codec k handle kept]\\\\n   210\\\\t    (or (get-in @found [:of k])\\\\n   211\\\\t        (let [portable (portable-cursor codec kept)\\\\n   212\\\\t              marker (when portable (lift-marker serve! handle))]\\\\n   213\\\\t          (when (and portable marker)\\\\n   214\\\\t            (let [cid (keyword \\\\\\\"yin.k\\\\\\\" (str \\\\\\\"c-\\\\\\\" (count (:cells @found))))\\\\n   215\\\\t                  cell {:yin.k/stream marker, :yin.k/position portable}]\\\\n   216\\\\t              (swap! found #(-> % (assoc-in [:of k] cid)\\\\n   217\\\\t                                (assoc-in [:cells cid] cell)))\\\\n   218\\\\t              cid))))))\\\\n   219\\\\t\\\\n   220\\\\t\\\\n   221\\\\t(defn- cursor-cell\\\\n   222\\\\t  \\\\\\\"The engine cursor cell a `:next` entry waits on: `:cursor-ref`'s\\\\n   223\\\\t   id into `:resources`, the cursor entry carrying the stream id and\\\\n   224\\\\t   the kept cursor (`vm/cursor-entry`). nil when it names nothing.\\\\\\\"\\\\n   225\\\\t  [resources entry]\\\\n   226\\\\t  (let [cid (get-in entry [:cursor-ref :id])\\\\n   227\\\\t        cell (get resources cid)]\\\\n   228\\\\t    (when (and (some? cid) (map? cell) (contains? cell :stream-id))\\\\n   229\\\\t      {:id cid, :stream-id (:stream-id cell), :cursor (:cursor cell)})))\\\\n   230\\\\t\\\\n   231\\\\t\\\\n   232\\\\t(defn- cell-identity\\\\n   233\\\\t  \\\\\\\"The stream identity a `:yin.k/cells` entry names, for a refusal\\\\n   234\\\\t   that names it even when the cell itself never lowered.\\\\\\\"\\\\n   235\\\\t  [cells cell-id]\\\\n   236\\\\t  (get-in cells [cell-id :yin.k/stream :dao.stream/identity]))\\\\n   237\\\\t\\\\n   238\\\\t\\\\n   239\\\\t;; =============================================================================\\\\n   240\\\\t;; Lift: one variant each\\\\n   241\\\\t;; =============================================================================\\\\n   242\\\\t\\\\n   243\\\\t(defn- lift-read\\\\n   244\\\\t  \\\\\\\"S7.4.3's blocked read: the cell `mint` gives for the entry's\\\\n   245\\\\t   cursor cell, at its kept position.\\\\\\\"\\\\n   246\\\\t  [resources mint codec entry]\\\\n   247\\\\t  (if-let [cell (cursor-cell resources entry)]\\\\n   248\\\\t    (if-let [cid (mint codec (:id cell)\\\\n   249\\\\t                       (get resources (:stream-id cell))\\\\n   250\\\\t                       (:cursor cell))]\\\\n   251\\\\t      {:pending {:yin.k/reason :next, :yin.k/cell cid}, :cell? true}\\\\n   252\\\\t      (unsatisfied (local-identity (get resources (:stream-id cell)))))\\\\n   253\\\\t    (unsatisfied)))\\\\n   254\\\\t\\\\n   255\\\\t\\\\n   256\\\\t(defn- lift-response-wait\\\\n   257\\\\t  \\\\\\\"S7.4.3's sent call: a `:next` entry carrying `:call-id`, the\\\\n   258\\\\t   response wait `semantic-restore` rebuilds -- the call's\\\\n   259\\\\t   correlation beside the response cell at its kept position, so\\\\n   260\\\\t   round-order on the cell is preserved on the resumer (S7.4.3).\\\\n   261\\\\t   The call's `:op` rides when the entry carries it (the engine's\\\\n   262\\\\t   own response wait does not; a caller assembling the frame takes\\\\n   263\\\\t   it from the call's parked record).\\\\\\\"\\\\n   264\\\\t  [resources mint codec entry]\\\\n   265\\\\t  (if-let [cell (cursor-cell resources entry)]\\\\n   266\\\\t    (if-let [cid (mint codec (:id cell)\\\\n   267\\\\t                       (get resources (:stream-id cell))\\\\n   268\\\\t                       (:cursor cell))]\\\\n   269\\\\t      {:pending (cond-> {:yin.k/reason :ffi,\\\\n   270\\\\t                         :yin.k/call-id (:call-id entry),\\\\n   271\\\\t                         :yin.k/cell cid}\\\\n   272\\\\t                  (contains? entry :op) (assoc :yin.k/op (:op entry))),\\\\n   273\\\\t       :cell? true}\\\\n   274\\\\t      (unsatisfied (local-identity (get resources (:stream-id cell)))))\\\\n   275\\\\t    (unsatisfied)))\\\\n   276\\\\t\\\\n   277\\\\t\\\\n   278\\\\t(defn- lift-write\\\\n   279\\\\t  \\\\\\\"S7.4.3's blocked write: the target stream's marker and the\\\\n   280\\\\t   retained `:datom` -- the value a retry appends, without which the\\\\n   281\\\\t   wait is not re-establishable. A put names a stream, never a\\\\n   282\\\\t   cursor cell.\\\\\\\"\\\\n   283\\\\t  [serve! resources entry]\\\\n   284\\\\t  (let [h (get resources (:stream-id entry))]\\\\n   285\\\\t    (if-let [marker (lift-marker serve! h)]\\\\n   286\\\\t      {:pending {:yin.k/reason :put,\\\\n   287\\\\t                 :yin.k/stream marker,\\\\n   288\\\\t                 :yin.k/value (:datom entry)}}\\\\n   289\\\\t      (unsatisfied (local-identity h)))))\\\\n   290\\\\t\\\\n   291\\\\t\\\\n   292\\\\t(defn- lift-retained-request\\\\n   293\\\\t  \\\\\\\"S7.4.3's retained call: a `:put` entry carrying `:request-sent`,\\\\n   294\\\\t   the request the engine holds unsent. The request stream's marker\\\\n   295\\\\t   is served, and `:request-op` and `:request-args` are read out of\\\\n   296\\\\t   the retained envelope so a resumer rebuilds it verbatim under the\\\\n   297\\\\t   call id. No response marker and no cell: a retained request has\\\\n   298\\\\t   neither -- the engine's response wait exists only once a request\\\\n   299\\\\t   has landed, which is the `:ffi` variant.\\\\\\\"\\\\n   300\\\\t  [serve! resources entry]\\\\n   301\\\\t  (let [h (get resources (:stream-id entry))\\\\n   302\\\\t        envelope (:datom entry)]\\\\n   303\\\\t    (if-let [marker (lift-marker serve! h)]\\\\n   304\\\\t      {:pending {:yin.k/reason :ffi-request,\\\\n   305\\\\t                 :yin.k/call-id (:call-id entry),\\\\n   306\\\\t                 :yin.k/request-op (or (apply2/request-op envelope)\\\\n   307\\\\t                                       (:op entry)),\\\\n   308\\\\t                 :yin.k/request-args (apply2/request-args envelope),\\\\n   309\\\\t                 :yin.k/request marker}}\\\\n   310\\\\t      (unsatisfied (local-identity h)))))\\\\n   311\\\\t\\\\n   312\\\\t\\\\n   313\\\\t(defn- lift-link\\\\n   314\\\\t  \\\\\\\"S7.4.3's link variants: the link pair are resource ids into the\\\\n   315\\\\t   machine's `:resources`, and the kept `:cursor` on the response\\\\n   316\\\\t   stream (`module/require-handler` mints it before the envelope is\\\\n   317\\\\t   appended) is the response cell -- a cell like any other, at its\\\\n   318\\\\t   kept position. Both pair markers travel, the engine's\\\\n   319\\\\t   `:link-response` entry retaining its `:request` beside the\\\\n   320\\\\t   response side; the envelope rides verbatim on the request-in-hand\\\\n   321\\\\t   variant.\\\\\\\"\\\\n   322\\\\t  [serve! resources mint codec entry]\\\\n   323\\\\t  (let [reason (:reason entry)\\\\n   324\\\\t        resp-h (get resources (:response entry))\\\\n   325\\\\t        req-h (get resources (:request entry))\\\\n   326\\\\t        kept (:cursor entry)]\\\\n   327\\\\t    (if-let [cid (mint codec [(:response entry) kept] resp-h kept)]\\\\n   328\\\\t      (let [resp (lift-marker serve! resp-h)\\\\n   329\\\\t            req (lift-marker serve! req-h)]\\\\n   330\\\\t        (if (and resp req)\\\\n   331\\\\t          {:pending (cond-> {:yin.k/reason reason,\\\\n   332\\\\t                             :yin.k/link-id (:link-id entry),\\\\n   333\\\\t                             :yin.k/name (:name entry),\\\\n   334\\\\t                             :yin.k/request req,\\\\n   335\\\\t                             :yin.k/response resp,\\\\n   336\\\\t                             :yin.k/cell cid}\\\\n   337\\\\t                      (= :link-request reason)\\\\n   338\\\\t                      (assoc :yin.k/envelope (:envelope entry))),\\\\n   339\\\\t           :cell? true}\\\\n   340\\\\t          (unsatisfied (local-identity (or req-h resp-h)))))\\\\n   341\\\\t      (unsatisfied (local-identity resp-h)))))\\\\n   342\\\\t\\\\n   343\\\\t\\\\n   344\\\\t(defn- lift-one\\\\n   345\\\\t  \\\\\\\"One pending entry of S7.4.3, lifted into `{:pending data,\\\\n   346\\\\t   :cell? bool}` -- `:cell?` true when the variant names a cursor\\\\n   347\\\\t   cell, which is what puts `:dao.stream.remote/v1` in\\\\n   348\\\\t   `:yin.k/cursor-profiles` -- or an outcome carrying\\\\n   349\\\\t   `:yin.k/status`: `:yin.k/unsatisfied` when a stream cannot be\\\\n   350\\\\t   served or a kept cursor does not survive the codec round trip;\\\\n   351\\\\t   `:yin.k/undecodable`, naming the reason, when the entry is no\\\\n   352\\\\t   variant at all.\\\\\\\"\\\\n   353\\\\t  [serve! resources mint codec entry]\\\\n   354\\\\t  (case (:reason entry)\\\\n   355\\\\t    :next\\\\n   356\\\\t    (if (:call-id entry)\\\\n   357\\\\t      (lift-response-wait resources mint codec entry)\\\\n   358\\\\t      (lift-read resources mint codec entry))\\\\n   359\\\\t\\\\n   360\\\\t    :put\\\\n   361\\\\t    (if (:request-sent entry)\\\\n   362\\\\t      (lift-retained-request serve! resources entry)\\\\n   363\\\\t      (lift-write serve! resources entry))\\\\n   364\\\\t\\\\n   365\\\\t    :link-request (lift-link serve! resources mint codec entry)\\\\n   366\\\\t\\\\n   367\\\\t    :link-response (lift-link serve! resources mint codec entry)\\\\n   368\\\\t\\\\n   369\\\\t    :install\\\\n   370\\\\t    {:pending {:yin.k/reason :install, :yin.k/name (:name entry)}}\\\\n   371\\\\t\\\\n   372\\\\t    {:yin.k/status :yin.k/undecodable, :yin.k/reason (:reason entry)}))\\\\n   373\\\\t\\\\n   374\\\\t\\\\n   375\\\\t;; =============================================================================\\\\n   376\\\\t;; Lift: the frame and the single entry\\\\n   377\\\\t;; =============================================================================\\\\n   378\\\\t\\\\n   379\\\\t(defn lift-frame\\\\n   380\\\\t  \\\\\\\"A whole frame set of S7.4.3 pending entries, lifted together:\\\\n   381\\\\t   `{:yin.k/pending [data ...], :yin.k/cells {cell-id cell},\\\\n   382\\\\t   :yin.k/requires requires}` on success -- the cells minted across\\\\n   383\\\\t   the WHOLE set, so two waiters on one engine cursor cell lift to\\\\n   384\\\\t   one UCF cell (S7.5.3) and `:dao.stream.remote/v1` rides in\\\\n   385\\\\t   `:yin.k/cursor-profiles` when any entry names a cell; the S7.9\\\\n   386\\\\t   `:yin.k/unsatisfied` outcome, naming the stream identity where one\\\\n   387\\\\t   is known, when any entry's stream cannot be served or its kept\\\\n   388\\\\t   cursor does not survive the codec round trip; the S7.9\\\\n   389\\\\t   `:yin.k/undecodable` outcome when any entry names no variant.\\\\n   390\\\\t   Failure is total (S7.5.4): a refused leaf refuses the frame.\\\\\\\"\\\\n   391\\\\t  ([serve! resources entries]\\\\n   392\\\\t   (lift-frame serve! resources entries cursor-codec))\\\\n   393\\\\t  ([serve! resources entries codec]\\\\n   394\\\\t   (let [found (atom {:cells {}, :of {}})\\\\n   395\\\\t         mint (mint-cell serve! found)\\\\n   396\\\\t         lifted (mapv #(lift-one serve! resources mint codec %) entries)]\\\\n   397\\\\t     (if-let [refusal (some #(when (contains? % :yin.k/status) %) lifted)]\\\\n   398\\\\t       refusal\\\\n   399\\\\t       {:yin.k/pending (mapv :pending lifted),\\\\n   400\\\\t        :yin.k/cells (:cells @found),\\\\n   401\\\\t        :yin.k/requires (if (some :cell? lifted) requires {})}))))\\\\n   402\\\\t\\\\n   403\\\\t\\\\n   404\\\\t(defn lift-pending\\\\n   405\\\\t  \\\\\\\"One pending entry of S7.4.3, lifted into its own self-contained\\\\n   406\\\\t   cell table: `{:yin.k/pending data, :yin.k/cells {cell-id cell},\\\\n   407\\\\t   :yin.k/requires requires}` on success, with the same `:yin.k/\\\\n   408\\\\t   unsatisfied` and `:yin.k/undecodable` outcomes `lift-frame`\\\\n   409\\\\t   gives. Frame assembly that shares cells across entries is\\\\n   410\\\\t   `lift-frame`'s.\\\\\\\"\\\\n   411\\\\t  ([serve! resources entry]\\\\n   412\\\\t   (lift-pending serve! resources entry cursor-codec))\\\\n   413\\\\t  ([serve! resources entry codec]\\\\n   414\\\\t   (let [r (lift-frame serve! resources [entry] codec)]\\\\n   415\\\\t     (if (contains? r :yin.k/status)\\\\n   416\\\\t       r\\\\n   417\\\\t       (assoc r :yin.k/pending (first (:yin.k/pending r)))))))\\\\n   418\\\\t\\\\n   419\\\\t\\\\n   420\\\\t;; =============================================================================\\\\n   421\\\\t;; Lower: back into resources and a wait-set entry\\\\n   422\\\\t;; =============================================================================\\\\n   423\\\\t\\\\n   424\\\\t(defn- stream-id-of\\\\n   425\\\\t  \\\\\\\"The fresh resource id the reflection of the stream `identity`\\\\n   426\\\\t   names stands under: derived from the identity, so two markers of\\\\n   427\\\\t   one stream attach once and lower shared. A receiver composing\\\\n   428\\\\t   these entries into a live `:resources` table re-keys them -- the\\\\n   429\\\\t   ids are fresh for the lowered state, the remap mechanical.\\\\\\\"\\\\n   430\\\\t  [identity]\\\\n   431\\\\t  (keyword \\\\\\\"yin.k\\\\\\\" (str \\\\\\\"s-\\\\\\\" identity)))\\\\n   432\\\\t\\\\n   433\\\\t\\\\n   434\\\\t(defn- pending-markers\\\\n   435\\\\t  \\\\\\\"Every stream marker `pending` names beside its cells' -- the\\\\n   436\\\\t   target of a put, the request of a retained call, the pair of a\\\\n   437\\\\t   link request.\\\\\\\"\\\\n   438\\\\t  [pending]\\\\n   439\\\\t  (case (:yin.k/reason pending)\\\\n   440\\\\t    :put [(:yin.k/stream pending)]\\\\n   441\\\\t    :ffi-request [(:yin.k/request pending)]\\\\n   442\\\\t    (:link-request :link-response)\\\\n   443\\\\t    [(:yin.k/request pending)\\\\n   444\\\\t     (:yin.k/response pending)]\\\\n   445\\\\t    []))\\\\n   446\\\\t\\\\n   447\\\\t\\\\n   448\\\\t(defn- attach-all\\\\n   449\\\\t  \\\\\\\"One attach per distinct stream identity, each ok installing its\\\\n   450\\\\t   reflection under `stream-id-of`'s fresh resource id. The first\\\\n   451\\\\t   attach that does not answer ok -- a reflection marked gone\\\\n   452\\\\t   included -- refuses the lower as `:yin.k/unsatisfied` naming that\\\\n   453\\\\t   identity.\\\\\\\"\\\\n   454\\\\t  [attach! markers]\\\\n   455\\\\t  (let [by-id (reduce (fn [m mkr]\\\\n   456\\\\t                        (update m (:dao.stream/identity mkr) #(or % mkr)))\\\\n   457\\\\t                      {} markers)]\\\\n   458\\\\t    (reduce-kv (fn [acc identity mkr]\\\\n   459\\\\t                 (if-let [h (lower-marker attach! mkr)]\\\\n   460\\\\t                   (let [sid (stream-id-of identity)]\\\\n   461\\\\t                     (-> acc\\\\n   462\\\\t                         (assoc-in [:streams identity] sid)\\\\n   463\\\\t                         (assoc-in [:resources sid] h)))\\\\n   464\\\\t                   (reduced (unsatisfied identity))))\\\\n   465\\\\t               {:streams {}, :resources {}}\\\\n   466\\\\t               by-id)))\\\\n   467\\\\t\\\\n   468\\\\t\\\\n   469\\\\t(defn- cell-resources\\\\n   470\\\\t  \\\\\\\"The fresh cursor entry each UCF cell lowers to: its carried\\\\n   471\\\\t   position, on the reflection of the stream the cell names, under\\\\n   472\\\\t   the cell id itself -- two references to one cell share the one\\\\n   473\\\\t   entry, and one ref per cell keeps its own (S7.5.3).\\\\\\\"\\\\n   474\\\\t  [streams cells]\\\\n   475\\\\t  (into {}\\\\n   476\\\\t        (map (fn [[cid cell]]\\\\n   477\\\\t               [cid {:stream-id (streams (cell-identity cells cid)),\\\\n   478\\\\t                     :cursor (:yin.k/position cell)}]))\\\\n   479\\\\t        cells))\\\\n   480\\\\t\\\\n   481\\\\t\\\\n   482\\\\t(defn- lower-one\\\\n   483\\\\t  \\\\\\\"One pending of S7.4.3, lowered: `{:entry e}` -- the wait-set\\\\n   484\\\\t   entry the receiver parks, the caller's register context `ctx`\\\\n   485\\\\t   merged verbatim under the stream and cell fields the data\\\\n   486\\\\t   rebuilds -- or an outcome carrying `:yin.k/status`, naming the\\\\n   487\\\\t   stream identity where one is known.\\\\\\\"\\\\n   488\\\\t  [pending ctx streams cells]\\\\n   489\\\\t  (case (:yin.k/reason pending)\\\\n   490\\\\t    :next\\\\n   491\\\\t    (let [cid (:yin.k/cell pending)]\\\\n   492\\\\t      (if-let [sid (streams (cell-identity cells cid))]\\\\n   493\\\\t        {:entry (merge ctx\\\\n   494\\\\t                       {:reason :next,\\\\n   495\\\\t                        :stream-id sid,\\\\n   496\\\\t                        :cursor-ref {:type :cursor-ref, :id cid}})}\\\\n   497\\\\t        (unsatisfied (cell-identity cells cid))))\\\\n   498\\\\t\\\\n   499\\\\t    :put\\\\n   500\\\\t    (if-let [sid (streams (get-in pending [:yin.k/stream\\\\n   501\\\\t                                           :dao.stream/identity]))]\\\\n   502\\\\t      {:entry (merge ctx\\\\n   503\\\\t                     {:reason :put,\\\\n   504\\\\t                      :stream-id sid,\\\\n   505\\\\t                      :datom (:yin.k/value pending)})}\\\\n   506\\\\t      (unsatisfied (get-in pending [:yin.k/stream :dao.stream/identity])))\\\\n   507\\\\t\\\\n   508\\\\t    :ffi\\\\n   509\\\\t    (let [cid (:yin.k/cell pending)]\\\\n   510\\\\t      (if-let [sid (streams (cell-identity cells cid))]\\\\n   511\\\\t        {:entry (merge ctx\\\\n   512\\\\t                       (cond-> {:reason :next,\\\\n   513\\\\t                                :call-id (:yin.k/call-id pending),\\\\n   514\\\\t                                :stream-id sid,\\\\n   515\\\\t                                :cursor-ref {:type :cursor-ref, :id cid}}\\\\n   516\\\\t                         (contains? pending :yin.k/op)\\\\n   517\\\\t                         (assoc :op (:yin.k/op pending))))}\\\\n   518\\\\t        (unsatisfied (cell-identity cells cid))))\\\\n   519\\\\t\\\\n   520\\\\t    :ffi-request\\\\n   521\\\\t    (if-let [sid (streams (get-in pending [:yin.k/request\\\\n   522\\\\t                                           :dao.stream/identity]))]\\\\n   523\\\\t      {:entry (merge ctx\\\\n   524\\\\t                     {:reason :put,\\\\n   525\\\\t                      :request-sent true,\\\\n   526\\\\t                      :call-id (:yin.k/call-id pending),\\\\n   527\\\\t                      :op (:yin.k/request-op pending),\\\\n   528\\\\t                      :stream-id sid,\\\\n   529\\\\t                      :datom (apply2/request (:yin.k/call-id pending)\\\\n   530\\\\t                                             (:yin.k/request-op pending)\\\\n   531\\\\t                                             (:yin.k/request-args\\\\n   532\\\\t                                               pending))})}\\\\n   533\\\\t      (unsatisfied (get-in pending [:yin.k/request :dao.stream/identity])))\\\\n   534\\\\t\\\\n   535\\\\t    (:link-request :link-response)\\\\n   536\\\\t    (let [reason (:yin.k/reason pending)\\\\n   537\\\\t          cid (:yin.k/cell pending)\\\\n   538\\\\t          sid (streams (cell-identity cells cid))\\\\n   539\\\\t          req (streams (get-in pending [:yin.k/request\\\\n   540\\\\t                                        :dao.stream/identity]))]\\\\n   541\\\\t      (if (and sid req)\\\\n   542\\\\t        {:entry (merge ctx\\\\n   543\\\\t                       (cond-> {:reason reason,\\\\n   544\\\\t                                :link-id (:yin.k/link-id pending),\\\\n   545\\\\t                                :name (:yin.k/name pending),\\\\n   546\\\\t                                :request req,\\\\n   547\\\\t                                :response sid,\\\\n   548\\\\t                                :cursor (:yin.k/position (get cells cid))}\\\\n   549\\\\t                         (= :link-request reason)\\\\n   550\\\\t                         (assoc :envelope (:yin.k/envelope pending))))}\\\\n   551\\\\t        (unsatisfied (cell-identity cells cid))))\\\\n   552\\\\t\\\\n   553\\\\t    :install\\\\n   554\\\\t    {:entry (merge ctx\\\\n   555\\\\t                   {:reason :install, :name (:yin.k/name pending)})}\\\\n   556\\\\t\\\\n   557\\\\t    {:yin.k/status :yin.k/undecodable,\\\\n   558\\\\t     :yin.k/reason (:yin.k/reason pending)}))\\\\n   559\\\\t\\\\n   560\\\\t\\\\n   561\\\\t(defn lower-frame\\\\n   562\\\\t  \\\\\\\"A whole frame set of S7.4.3 pendings, lowered together:\\\\n   563\\\\t   `{:entries [e ...], :resources table}` -- one fresh stream entry\\\\n   564\\\\t   per distinct served identity and one fresh cursor entry per\\\\n   565\\\\t   distinct UCF cell, two waiters on one cell lowering back into one\\\\n   566\\\\t   shared entry and independent cells staying independent (S7.5.3) --\\\\n   567\\\\t   with the same `:yin.k/unsatisfied` and `:yin.k/undecodable`\\\\n   568\\\\t   outcomes `lift-frame` gives. `contexts`, parallel to `pendings`,\\\\n   569\\\\t   is each entry's register context, merged verbatim.\\\\\\\"\\\\n   570\\\\t  [attach! pendings cells contexts]\\\\n   571\\\\t  (let [ms (distinct (remove nil?\\\\n   572\\\\t                             (concat (map :yin.k/stream (vals cells))\\\\n   573\\\\t                                     (mapcat pending-markers pendings))))\\\\n   574\\\\t        a (attach-all attach! ms)]\\\\n   575\\\\t    (if (contains? a :yin.k/status)\\\\n   576\\\\t      a\\\\n   577\\\\t      (let [lowered (mapv #(lower-one %1 %2 (:streams a) cells)\\\\n   578\\\\t                          pendings contexts)]\\\\n   579\\\\t        (if-let [refusal (some #(when (contains? % :yin.k/status) %)\\\\n   580\\\\t                               lowered)]\\\\n   581\\\\t          refusal\\\\n   582\\\\t          {:entries (mapv :entry lowered),\\\\n   583\\\\t           :resources (merge (:resources a)\\\\n   584\\\\t                             (cell-resources (:streams a) cells))})))))\\\\n   585\\\\t\\\\n   586\\\\t\\\\n   587\\\\t(defn lower-pending\\\\n   588\\\\t  \\\\\\\"One pending entry of S7.4.3, lowered: `{:entry e, :resources\\\\n   589\\\\t   table}` -- the wait-set entry `ctx`'s registers ride on, and the\\\\n   590\\\\t   fresh resource entries it polls through -- with the same\\\\n   591\\\\t   `:yin.k/unsatisfied` and `:yin.k/undecodable` outcomes\\\\n   592\\\\t   `lower-frame` gives. Frame assembly that shares cursor entries\\\\n   593\\\\t   across entries is `lower-frame`'s.\\\\\\\"\\\\n   594\\\\t  [attach! pending cells ctx]\\\\n   595\\\\t  (let [r (lower-frame attach! [pending] cells [ctx])]\\\\n   596\\\\t    (if (contains? r :yin.k/status)\\\\n   597\\\\t      r\\\\n   598\\\\t      (-> r\\\\n   599\\\\t          (assoc :entry (first (:entries r)))\\\\n   600\\\\t          (dissoc :entries)))))\\\\n\\\",\\\"exit_code\\\":0,\\\"status\\\":\\\"completed\\\"}}\\n{\\\"type\\\":\\\"item.started\\\",\\\"item\\\":{\\\"id\\\":\\\"item_4\\\",\\\"type\\\":\\\"command_execution\\\",\\\"command\\\":\\\"/bin/zsh -lc 'cat collab/1790522280000-vm-engineer-dao-stream-remote-slice8-fixes.prompt.md'\\\",\\\"aggregated_output\\\":\\