     (-> r\\\\n   599\\\\t          (assoc :entry (first (:entries r)))\\\\n   600\\\\t          (dissoc :entries)))))\\\\n\\\",\\\"exit_code\\\":0,\\\"status\\\":\\\"completed\\\"}}\\n{\\\"type\\\":\\\"item.started\\\",\\\"item\\\":{\\\"id\\\":\\\"item_12\\\",\\\"type\\\":\\\"command_execution\\\",\\\"command\\\":\\\"/bin/zsh -lc \\\\\\\"rg -n '7\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\.4\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\.3|7\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\.5\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\.3|7\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\.11|ffi-request|link-request' docs/design/yin.vm.universal-continuation-format.md\\\\\\\"\\\",\\\"aggregated_output\\\":\\\"\\\",\\\"exit_code\\\":null,\\\"status\\\":\\\"in_progress\\\"}}\\n{\\\"type\\\":\\\"item.completed\\\",\\\"item\\\":{\\\"id\\\":\\\"item_12\\\",\\\"type\\\":\\\"command_execution\\\",\\\"command\\\":\\\"/bin/zsh -lc \\\\\\\"rg -n '7\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\.4\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\.3|7\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\.5\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\.3|7\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\.11|ffi-request|link-request' docs/design/yin.vm.universal-continuation-format.md\\\\\\\"\\\",\\\"aggregated_output\\\":\\\"10:> S7.11 lists the acceptance blockers that keep this warning standing until\\\\n36:(S7.6.1); S7.11 records the remaining definition-frame obligations.\\\\n45:Every sentence in §7.2–§7.9 is a rule of the proposed protocol. §7.11 records\\\\n78:(sharing thresholds differ, §7.5.3), so the encodings address differently,\\\\n109: :yin.k/values      {…}                        ; §7.5.3  shared subvalues, by content address\\\\n110: :yin.k/cells       {…}                        ; §7.5.3  cursor cells: logical identity + position\\\\n303:transition; see the revision log in S7.11. The de Bruijn images carry\\\\n344:obligation: both must yield the same image, and a test in the harness (§7.11)\\\\n385:encodings legitimately differ (§7.5.3), so `:yin.k/id` is *not* what custody,\\\\n437:                                          ; | :ffi-request | :call-effect\\\\n438:                                          ; | :link-request | :link-response\\\\n440: :yin.k/val      nil           